-0876d2b3638a" :step/content "question-03601169-5838-5406-9812-fc2ccaab4423" :step/next "step-4096c219-d4f7-5387-84d1-ee267dbd82e4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4096c219-d4f7-5387-84d1-ee267dbd82e4" :step/id #uuid "4096c219-d4f7-5387-84d1-ee267dbd82e4" :step/content "question-768c8258-584d-53be-9ed2-7212820baebf" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138444 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0ba5f5a5-9aa0-5b4c-ab5c-6490e52ab690"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0ba5f5a5-9aa0-5b4c-ab5c-6490e52ab690" :question/id #uuid "0ba5f5a5-9aa0-5b4c-ab5c-6490e52ab690" :question/math-academy-id "q-46125" :question/problem "A car travels at $1\\,000$ meters per minute. In kilometers, how far will the car travel in one hour?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the units $\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{min}},$ and we want to convert this into $\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{hour}}.$ We're converting two units instead of just one, so we're going to have to multiply by two conversion factors:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{min}}\\cdot \\,\\frac{?}{?}\\cdot \\,\\frac{?}{?}=\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{hour}}\n$$\n\nOne of the conversion factors should change $\\text{m}$ to $\\text{km}.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{m}}}{\\text{min}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{km}}{\\cancel{\\text{m}}}\\cdot \\,\\frac{?}{?}=\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{hour}}\n$$\n\nThe other conversion factor should change $\\text{min}$ into $\\text{hour}.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{m}}}{\\cancel{\\text{min}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{km}}{\\cancel{\\text{m}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\text{min}}}{\\text{hour}}=\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{hour}}\n$$\n\nSo, our conversion formula is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{min}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{m}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{min}}{\\text{hour}}=\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{hour}}.\n$$\n\nNow that we have our conversion formula, we need to determine the correct numbers to use, and apply it.\n\n- The rate given in the problem statement is $1\\,000\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{min}}.$\n\n- There are $1\\,000$ meters per kilometer, therefore, there are $\\frac{1}{1\\,000}$ kilometers per meter.\n\n- There are $60$ minutes in one hour.\n\nApplying our conversion formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1000\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{min}} & =1000\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{min}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1\\,000}\\,\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{m}}\\cdot 60\\,\\frac{\\text{min}}{\\text{hour}} \\\\  & =1000\\cdot \\frac{1}{1\\,000}\\cdot 60(\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{m}}}{\\cancel{\\text{min}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{km}}{\\cancel{\\text{m}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\text{min}}}{\\text{hour}}) \\\\  & =60\\,\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{hour}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, a speed of $1\\,000$ meters per minute is equivalent to $60$ kilometers per hour. Thus, the car will travel $60$ kilometers in one hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e6520f1e-9ae6-59fe-87c3-d43c3f601aa8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e6520f1e-9ae6-59fe-87c3-d43c3f601aa8" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6520f1e-9ae6-59fe-87c3-d43c3f601aa8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-946da25e-7b93-5445-8eab-d777e9ef8c7f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-877592ad-d32e-5675-857f-189b5845548a" "answer-7deb7461-5433-56db-95dd-78442f6e315f" "answer-2fddd4a0-4f7c-55f3-991c-800d86dfbd7b" "answer-946da25e-7b93-5445-8eab-d777e9ef8c7f" "answer-6ed443d5-d3c4-573e-a0a0-2e968d29aec6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-877592ad-d32e-5675-857f-189b5845548a" :answer/id #uuid "877592ad-d32e-5675-857f-189b5845548a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100\\,\\text{km}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7deb7461-5433-56db-95dd-78442f6e315f" :answer/id #uuid "7deb7461-5433-56db-95dd-78442f6e315f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\,\\text{km}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fddd4a0-