statement $(T∨T)∧(U∧U).$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that:\n\n- the expression $T∨T$ simplifies to just $T,$ and\n\n- the expression $U∧U$ simplifies to just $U.$\n\nSo, the given statement can be simplified to\n\n$$\nT∧U.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5611a03b-de4a-5f28-9718-ae6fa01eeede"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5611a03b-de4a-5f28-9718-ae6fa01eeede" :answer-field/id #uuid "5611a03b-de4a-5f28-9718-ae6fa01eeede" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-07ff8a65-e08b-5ffb-8da9-21a3874a08dd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-29fb1ac7-393d-5817-a11c-168e81bf03fa" "answer-5b75c300-b64a-502b-88fa-177302ac2af6" "answer-07ff8a65-e08b-5ffb-8da9-21a3874a08dd" "answer-f2e8bfca-4d92-5a07-a6ea-363df0d292f5" "answer-2b876056-b3ea-5303-a9dc-a6bda1b7736b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29fb1ac7-393d-5817-a11c-168e81bf03fa" :answer/id #uuid "29fb1ac7-393d-5817-a11c-168e81bf03fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(T∧U)∨U" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b75c300-b64a-502b-88fa-177302ac2af6" :answer/id #uuid "5b75c300-b64a-502b-88fa-177302ac2af6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(T∨U)∧U" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07ff8a65-e08b-5ffb-8da9-21a3874a08dd" :answer/id #uuid "07ff8a65-e08b-5ffb-8da9-21a3874a08dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T∧U" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2e8bfca-4d92-5a07-a6ea-363df0d292f5" :answer/id #uuid "f2e8bfca-4d92-5a07-a6ea-363df0d292f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T∨(T∧U)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b876056-b3ea-5303-a9dc-a6bda1b7736b" :answer/id #uuid "2b876056-b3ea-5303-a9dc-a6bda1b7736b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "T∨U" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198694 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-974d976d-65a4-5d23-86e7-77e1c81632fd" :question/id #uuid "974d976d-65a4-5d23-86e7-77e1c81632fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-170781" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $(Q∨R)∧(P∨P).$" :question/worked-solution "The expression $P∨P$ simplifies to just $P.$\n\nSo, the given statement can be simplified to\n\n$$\n(Q∨R)∧P.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f0c6bb96-b4df-5b06-b40b-3a6a8adba71d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f0c6bb96-b4df-5b06-b40b-3a6a8adba71d" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0c6bb96-b4df-5b06-b40b-3a6a8adba71d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-34373780-153a-5776-ad52-5d02082ccfa8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e33e1c64-3e75-51e2-a69d-9f41040a8281" "answer-34373780-153a-5776-ad52-5d02082ccfa8" "answer-a6aa55a2-920e-5757-b09a-bb0b60c1b87f" "answer-a2ff27c5-aae1-51e9-a0ad-5495650e14ea" "answer-bc9b4799-d2cc-5344-899c-412f238124d8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e33e1c64-3e75-51e2-a69d-9f41040a8281" :answer/id #uuid "e33e1c64-3e75-51e2-a69d-9f41040a8281" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(Q∧P)∨R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34373780-153a-5776-ad52-5d02082ccfa8" :answer/id #uuid "34373780-153a-5776-ad52-5d02082ccfa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(Q∨R)∧P" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6aa55a2-920e-5757-b09a-bb0b60c1b87f" :answer/id #uuid "a6aa55a2-920e-5757-b09a-bb0b60c1b87f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(Q∨R)∨P" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2ff27c5-aae1-51e9-a0ad-5495650e14ea" :answer/id #uuid "a2ff27c5-aae1-51e9-a0ad-5495650e14ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Q∨(R∧P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc9b4799-d2cc-5344-899c-412f238124d8" :answer/id #uuid "bc9b4799-d2cc-5344-899c-412f238124d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Q∨R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7ea98094-8950-5b20-861d-41decac9476c" :question/id #uuid "7ea98094-8950-5b20-861d-41decac9476c" :question/math-academy-id "q-170789" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $R∧(Q∨(Q∧Q)).$" :question/worked-solution "First, the expression $Q∧Q$ simplifies to just $Q.$ \n\nSo, the given statement can be simplified to \n\n$$\nR∧(Q∨Q).\n$$\n\nThen, the expression $Q∨Q$ simplifies to just $Q.$\n\nSo, the given statement can be simplified to \n\n$$\nR∧Q.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8670cfd6-f688-5e0c-ad34-bcc8a9380e86"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8670cfd6-f688-5e0c-ad34-bcc8a9380e86" :answer-field/id #uuid "8670cfd6-f688-5e0c-ad34-bcc8a9380e86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1a958a38-6801-58be-b387-50b13024ce7c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bc198b10-7372-56a8-a226-8b76f4d61f87" "answer-164f0918-fe41-5f2c-ae96-41edfe5a78a5" "answer-06d1900f-904c-5ce9-9af9-2a655214c6a5" "answer-1a958a38-6801-58be-b387-50b13024ce7c" "answer-fb6b08ff-4d48-556d-b3ab-c1591df39e88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc198b10-7372-56a8-a226-8b76f4d61f87" :answer/id #uuid "bc198b10-7372-56a8-a226-8b76f4d61f87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-164f0918-fe41-5f2c-ae96-41edfe5a78a5" :answer/id #uuid "164f0918-fe41-5f2c-ae96-41edfe5a78a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Q∧(R∨Q)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06d1900f-904c-5ce9-9af9-2a655214c6a5" :answer/id #uuid "06d1900f-904c-5ce9-9af9-2a655214c6a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a958a38-6801-58be-b387-50b13024ce7c" :answer/id #uuid "1a958a38-6801-58be-b387-50b13024ce7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R∧Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb6b08ff-4d48-556d-b3ab-c1591df39e88" :answer/id #uuid "fb6b08ff-4d48-556d-b3ab-c1591df39e88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R∨Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a5dc4674-bf70-593d-b79c-9ae4e2518f41" :question/id #uuid "a5dc4674-bf70-593d-b79c-9ae4e2518f41" :question/math-academy-id "q-170790" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $A∨(B∧(B∨B)).$" :question/worked-solution "First, the expression $B∨B$ simplifies to just $B.$\n\nSo, the given statement can be simplified to\n\n$$\nA∨(B∧B).\n$$\n\nThen, the expression $B∧B$ simplifies to just $B.$\n\nSo, the given statement can be simplified to\n\n$$\nA∨B.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5e77341c-73c0-5944-9e01-8bd2d9af7a60"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5e77341c-73c0-5944-9e01-8bd2d9af7a60" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e77341c-73c0-5944-9e01-8bd2d9af7a60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c6ef83b4-81d3-5ded-af82-d36051b69727" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6cefaf07-2cfa-5151-8157-c81d87efa699" "answer-44228842-34e1-5bf5-8d27-9053ac142914" "answer-c6ef83b4-81d3-5ded-af82-d36051b69727" "answer-8e47b951-af3a-5c88-ab72-2fa9b133034f" "answer-db4dfb95-d27c-5dec-80e4-a792d953f65a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cefaf07-2cfa-5151-8157-c81d87efa699" :answer/id #uuid "6cefaf07-2cfa-5151-8157-c81d87efa699" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44228842-34e1-5bf5-8d27-9053ac142914" :answer/id #uuid "44228842-34e1-5bf5-8d27-9053ac142914" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A∧B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6ef83b4-81d3-5ded-af82-d36051b69727" :answer/id #uuid "c6ef83b4-81d3-5ded-af82-d36051b69727" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A∨B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e47b951-af3a-5c88-ab72-2fa9b133034f" :answer/id #uuid "8e47b951-af3a-5c88-ab72-2fa9b133034f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db4dfb95-d27c-5dec-80e4-a792d953f65a" :answer/id #uuid "db4dfb95-d27c-5dec-80e4-a792d953f65a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B∨(A∧B)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199518 :tutorial/content "Recall that the statement \"$A$ and $B$\", represented symbolically as $A \\land B,$ is true if $A$ is true *and* $B$ is true. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nWe can represent all possible permutations of the truth values of $A$ and $B$ and the subsequent truth values of $A\\land B$ using a **truth table**:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A \\land B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n\nEach row of the truth table contains an input for $A,$ an input for $B,$ and the corresponding output for $A \\land B.$\n\n- The first row says that if $A$ is true and $B$ is true, then $A \\land B$ is true.\n\n- The second row says that if $A$ is true and $B$ is false, then $A \\land B$ is false.\n\n- The third row says that if $A$ is false and $B$ is true, then $A \\land B$ is false.\n\n- The fourth row says that if $A$ is false and $B$ is false, then $A \\land B$ is false." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199600 :tutorial/content "The statement \"$A$ or $B$,\" represented symbolically as $A \\lor B,$ is true if $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or both $A$ and $B$ are true. Otherwise, it is false. \n\nThe corresponding truth table is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A \\lor B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n\nAs we'll see, truth tables provide a convenient way to determine the truth values of complex logical statements. They can also be used to prove some mathematical theorems!" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199601 :tutorial/content "Consider the following statement:\n\n$$\nA \\land (B\\lor A)\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can use a truth table to calculate the truth values of this statement given all possible permutations of the truth values of $A$ and $B.$\n\nFirst, we complete a truth table for the part in parentheses, $B \\lor A.$  The statement $B \\lor A$ is true if either $A$ is true, $B$ is true, or both $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,B \\lor A\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n\nNext, we add a new column for $A \\land (B\\lor A).$ \n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,B \\lor A\\,$ | $\\,A \\land (B \\lor A)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |  |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |  |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |  |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |  |\n\nTo fill in the rows, we consider the truth values of $A$ and $(B\\lor A)$ and use this to determine the truth value of $A \\land (B\\lor A)$ in each case.\n\n- Consider the first row. Since $A$ is true and $(B\\lor A)$ is true, their conjunction $A \\land (B\\lor A)$ is *true*:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,B \\lor A\\,$ | $\\,A \\land (B \\lor A)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |  |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |  |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |  |\n\n- Next, consider the second row. Since $A$ is true and $(B\\lor A)$ is true, their conjunction $A \\land (B\\lor A)$ is *true*:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,B \\lor A\\,$ | $\\,A \\land (B \\lor A)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |  |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |  |\n\n- Now, consider the third row. Since $A$ is false and $(B\\lor A)$ is true, their conjunction $A \\land (B\\lor A)$ is *false*:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,B \\lor A\\,$ | $\\,A \\land (B \\lor A)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |  |\n\n- Finally, consider the fourth row. Since $A$ is false and $(B\\lor A)$ is false, their conjunction $A \\land (B\\lor A)$ is *false*:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,B \\lor A\\,$ | $\\,A \\land (B \\lor A)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n\nThe completed truth table is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,B \\lor A\\,$ | $\\,A \\land (B \\lor A)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199519 :tutorial/content "Two statements are **logically equivalent** if they have identical truth tables. \n\nA trivial logical equivalence is that every statement is logically equivalent to itself. We write this as follows:\n\n$$\nP \\equiv P\n$$\n\nTo prove this, we can use a truth table.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,P\\,$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n\nSince $P$ and $P$ have identical truth values, they're logically equivalent.\n\nAnother trivial equivalence is that the conjunction of a statement with itself is equivalent to the original statement.\n\n$$\nP \\land P \\equiv P\n$$\n\nFor example, the compound statement \"$x=3$ and $x=3$\" is logically equivalent to \"$x=3$\", which matches our intuition. \n\nAgain, we can prove the general result using a truth table.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,P \\land P\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n\nThe statements $P$ and $P\\land P$ are logically equivalent since they have identical truth values. \n\nWe also have the following logical equivalence for the disjunction of $P$ with itself.\n\n$$\nP \\lor P \\equiv P\n$$\n\nWe can justify this result using a truth table. \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,P \\lor P\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n\nThe statements $P$ and $P\\lor P$ are logically equivalent since they have identical truth values. \n\nCollectively, the results\n\n$$\nP\\land P \\equiv P ,\\qquad P\\lor P \\equiv P\n$$\n\nare known as the **idempotent laws.**" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198512 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059675 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-83b5db67-0cfd-59f0-8254-1d32998685fc" "question-94bfc6e6-a43f-5249-b046-4e95dd242cc6" "question-7c894a69-28f5-558a-ade7-8f7e7954ebf4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-83b5db67-0cfd-59f0-8254-1d32998685fc" :question/id #uuid "83b5db67-0cfd-59f0-8254-1d32998685fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-47984" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y=\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{3}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Applying this formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{3}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{3}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{3}+{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f4175479-f256-5ab9-9cfb-a0e3e88e6fa3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f4175479-f256-5ab9-9cfb-a0e3e88e6fa3" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4175479-f256-5ab9-9cfb-a0e3e88e6fa3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0e87bb41-37ec-51b0-90c2-386893952022" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ef209f1c-45b2-5eb0-a0b8-6f5c8266e247" "answer-64fa19fb-c747-568b-ad30-d38992d14797" "answer-e3c2ac7d-c4a5-557b-a3d6-dcd10f508d48" "answer-6d432d7e-6e29-58fd-8eee-cb46ac6ac7bd" "answer-0e87bb41-37ec-51b0-90c2-386893952022"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef209f1c-45b2-5eb0-a0b8-6f5c8266e247" :answer/id #uuid "ef209f1c-45b2-5eb0-a0b8-6f5c8266e247" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{3}+{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64fa19fb-c747-568b-ad30-d38992d14797" :answer/id #uuid "64fa19fb-c747-568b-ad30-d38992d14797" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3c2ac7d-c4a5-557b-a3d6-dcd10f508d48" :answer/id #uuid "e3c2ac7d-c4a5-557b-a3d6-dcd10f508d48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d432d7e-6e29-58fd-8eee-cb46ac6ac7bd" :answer/id #uuid "6d432d7e-6e29-58fd-8eee-cb46ac6ac7bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{3}+3{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e87bb41-37ec-51b0-90c2-386893952022" :answer/id #uuid "0e87bb41-37ec-51b0-90c2-386893952022" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{3}+{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-94bfc6e6-a43f-5249-b046-4e95dd242cc6" :question/id #uuid "94bfc6e6-a43f-5249-b046-4e95dd242cc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-30988" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}-11.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Applying this formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}-11) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-182c4a26-9e39-59c6-8813-cab2a16a0730"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-182c4a26-9e39-59c6-8813-cab2a16a0730" :answer-field/id #uuid "182c4a26-9e39-59c6-8813-cab2a16a0730" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9c379984-86b2-5382-ac5b-36f81eb2c38d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-42d8d3f1-b54f-5e7f-8d1d-0466a7bd27d1" "answer-ca8d5c20-cb81-5101-81a2-893618e67ba2" "answer-56c27e64-4407-52e3-8447-a30f78f42be9" "answer-9c379984-86b2-5382-ac5b-36f81eb2c38d" "answer-105d29a7-9a34-55b8-a94b-995812557ef4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42d8d3f1-b54f-5e7f-8d1d-0466a7bd27d1" :answer/id #uuid "42d8d3f1-b54f-5e7f-8d1d-0466a7bd27d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca8d5c20-cb81-5101-81a2-893618e67ba2" :answer/id #uuid "ca8d5c20-cb81-5101-81a2-893618e67ba2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56c27e64-4407-52e3-8447-a30f78f42be9" :answer/id #uuid "56c27e64-4407-52e3-8447-a30f78f42be9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c379984-86b2-5382-ac5b-36f81eb2c38d" :answer/id #uuid "9c379984-86b2-5382-ac5b-36f81eb2c38d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-105d29a7-9a34-55b8-a94b-995812557ef4" :answer/id #uuid "105d29a7-9a34-55b8-a94b-995812557ef4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}-11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7c894a69-28f5-558a-ade7-8f7e7954ebf4" :question/id #uuid "7c894a69-28f5-558a-ade7-8f7e7954ebf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-30987" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+8.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Applying this formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+8) \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\cdot 2x+0 \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-10x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8f8541fc-fa14-5f93-80a3-f994b1803ff3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8f8541fc-fa14-5f93-80a3-f994b1803ff3" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f8541fc-fa14-5f93-80a3-f994b1803ff3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3194e810-de8d-5ddb-b76b-c74b5e2ef41d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d3209c96-76c1-5e14-9703-6ac9f612067a" "answer-3194e810-de8d-5ddb-b76b-c74b5e2ef41d" "answer-f26b14ca-3532-5536-8a57-8073b5442eba" "answer-ab58c061-3981-52fa-bc50-c227c5cc414a" "answer-3f601fa8-b710-5fc9-9176-855a030771b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3209c96-76c1-5e14-9703-6ac9f612067a" :answer/id #uuid "d3209c96-76c1-5e14-9703-6ac9f612067a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3194e810-de8d-5ddb-b76b-c74b5e2ef41d" :answer/id #uuid "3194e810-de8d-5ddb-b76b-c74b5e2ef41d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-10x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f26b14ca-3532-5536-8a57-8073b5442eba" :answer/id #uuid "f26b14ca-3532-5536-8a57-8073b5442eba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab58c061-3981-52fa-bc50-c227c5cc414a" :answer/id #uuid "ab58c061-3981-52fa-bc50-c227c5cc414a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-10x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f601fa8-b710-5fc9-9176-855a030771b5" :answer/id #uuid "3f601fa8-b710-5fc9-9176-855a030771b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059676 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9b9f5ad2-fc37-5cb1-8895-57f56e806362" "question-75deedc5-439f-5c0b-9ed9-ea7f29313f69"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9b9f5ad2-fc37-5cb1-8895-57f56e806362" :question/id #uuid "9b9f5ad2-fc37-5cb1-8895-57f56e806362" :question/math-academy-id "q-341876" :question/problem "Calculate the instantaneous rate of change of the function $f(x)=6x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ when $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\n${f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change when $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is given by the value of the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ \n\nFirst, we compute the derivative, using the fact that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)=6.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x) \\\\  & =6-{sec}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =6-{sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =6-{(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})})}^{2} \\\\  & =6-{(\\frac{1}{1/2})}^{2} \\\\  & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-847db2ec-c888-5238-a1ba-407a230ec903"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-847db2ec-c888-5238-a1ba-407a230ec903" :answer-field/id #uuid "847db2ec-c888-5238-a1ba-407a230ec903" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4316991d-1d98-5261-b089-c06f2c337224" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4316991d-1d98-5261-b089-c06f2c337224"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4316991d-1d98-5261-b089-c06f2c337224" :answer/id #uuid "4316991d-1d98-5261-b089-c06f2c337224" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-75deedc5-439f-5c0b-9ed9-ea7f29313f69" :question/id #uuid "75deedc5-439f-5c0b-9ed9-ea7f29313f69" :question/math-academy-id "q-341826" :question/problem "Calculate the instantaneous rate of change of the function $f(x)=4x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ when $x=0.$\n\n${f}^{′}(0)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change when $x=0$ is given by the value of the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ at $x=0.$ \n\nFirst, we compute the derivative, using the fact that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x)=4.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x) \\\\  & =4-{sec}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =4-{sec}^{2}⁡(0) \\\\  & =4-{(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)})}^{2} \\\\  & =4-{(\\frac{1}{1})}^{2}=4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change is $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7b17d67a-7d81-5cb0-bd55-92bce57573b5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7b17d67a-7d81-5cb0-bd55-92bce57573b5" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b17d67a-7d81-5cb0-bd55-92bce57573b5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-47b44d8b-ac69-5abc-8c54-02ef7744ad3b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-47b44d8b-ac69-5abc-8c54-02ef7744ad3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47b44d8b-ac69-5abc-8c54-02ef7744ad3b" :answer/id #uuid "47b44d8b-ac69-5abc-8c54-02ef7744ad3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060893 :tutorial/content "The derivatives of sine, cosine, and tangent are shown in the table below:\n\n| $f(x)$ | $f'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $\\sin x$ | $\\cos x$ |\n| $\\cos x$ | $-\\sin x$ |\n| $\\tan x$ | $\\sec^2 x$ |\n\nNow that we know the derivatives of the standard trigonometric functions, we can differentiate any combination of them by using the properties of differentiation.\n\nFor example, let's find the derivative of $y = \\cos x + \\sin x.$\n\nHere, we can use the fact that the derivative of the sum is equal to the sum of the derivatives, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We'll derive the derivatives shown in the table at the end of this lesson." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060894 :tutorial/content "To understand why the derivative of sine is cosine, we need to use the definition of the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}} {\\textrm{d}x} (\\sin x) =  \\lim_{h\\rightarrow 0}\\dfrac{\\sin(x+h) - \\sin x}{h}\n$$\n\nNow, the so-called **addition formula for sine** states that\n\n$$\n\\sin(x+h) = \\sin(x)\\cos(h)+\\cos (x)  \\sin(h).\n$$\n\nBy using the addition formula for sine, we can rewrite our expression for the derivative as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(h)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(h)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(h)-1)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(h)}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(h)-1)}{h}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(h)}{h}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){{{lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(h)-1)}{h}}_{⏟}}_{0}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x){{{lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(h)}{h}}_{⏟}}_{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the last step, we used two important results for trigonometric limits:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{h\\rightarrow 0} \\dfrac{1 - \\cos(h)}{h}=0 \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad \\lim_{h\\rightarrow 0} \\dfrac{\\sin(h)}{h}=1.\n$$\n\nDeriving these results requires separate discussions, which we'll leave to future topics." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060895 :tutorial/content "We can follow the same method for the cosine and use the definition of the derivative to show that $(\\cos x)'=-\\sin x.$ First, we start with the definition of the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}} {\\textrm{d}x} (\\cos x) =  \\lim_{h\\rightarrow 0}\\dfrac{\\cos(x+h) - \\cos x}{h}\n$$\n\nNow, the so-called **addition formula for cosine** states that\n\n$$\n\\cos(x+h) = \\cos(x)\\cos(h)- \\sin(x)\\sin(h).\n$$\n\nUsing the addition formula for cosine, we can rewrite our expression for the derivative as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(h)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(h)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(h)-1)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(h)}{h} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x){{{lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(h)-1}{h}}_{⏟}}_{0}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){{{lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(h)}{h}}_{⏟}}_{1} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOnce again, in the last step, we used the special limits for sine and cosine." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059951 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119869 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b8283679-623f-5e9d-b3dc-5a2b30321fdc" "question-b2b0f174-efe7-5216-b895-6e427b351bde"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b8283679-623f-5e9d-b3dc-5a2b30321fdc" :question/id #uuid "b8283679-623f-5e9d-b3dc-5a2b30321fdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-35500" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d1e5821252dd0634c6033a35247af033bcda8a96fa3733b65be52565a60ea3a6.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of $f(x).$ Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\,-2}f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "As $x$ approaches $-2$ from the right, the function value $f(x)$ grows to infinity, and therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}f(x)=\\infty .\n$$\n\nHowever, as $x$ approaches $-2$ from the left, the function value $f(x)$ goes to $-\\infty$, and therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f1720c0f-a588-5d99-8985-6683833889bc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f1720c0f-a588-5d99-8985-6683833889bc" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1720c0f-a588-5d99-8985-6683833889bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ee732d08-29d7-5135-ba9f-9b7f75226b5f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-142e2e05-50df-5a66-9688-4af983efdc65" "answer-87134715-3e01-5440-bb15-b1ddf77a099a" "answer-4c0ad2b8-414d-5a17-bc60-4cf1f699f2a3" "answer-ee732d08-29d7-5135-ba9f-9b7f75226b5f" "answer-ef5f59d6-b28c-51ed-af43-017b89b043d7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-142e2e05-50df-5a66-9688-4af983efdc65" :answer/id #uuid "142e2e05-50df-5a66-9688-4af983efdc65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87134715-3e01-5440-bb15-b1ddf77a099a" :answer/id #uuid "87134715-3e01-5440-bb15-b1ddf77a099a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c0ad2b8-414d-5a17-bc60-4cf1f699f2a3" :answer/id #uuid "4c0ad2b8-414d-5a17-bc60-4cf1f699f2a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)=\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee732d08-29d7-5135-ba9f-9b7f75226b5f" :answer/id #uuid "ee732d08-29d7-5135-ba9f-9b7f75226b5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)=\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef5f59d6-b28c-51ed-af43-017b89b043d7" :answer/id #uuid "ef5f59d6-b28c-51ed-af43-017b89b043d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=-\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b2b0f174-efe7-5216-b895-6e427b351bde" :question/id #uuid "b2b0f174-efe7-5216-b895-6e427b351bde" :question/math-academy-id "q-51034" :question/problem "![](images/84/84490ed5dee30eb93ae322d0d4ca20109672a80083bf9eabb252ae49c7501036.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of $f(x).$ Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,5}f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "As $x$ approaches $5$ from the left, the function value $f(x)$ goes to $-\\infty$, and therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nHowever, the function is not defined for $x>5,$ and consequently, we cannot approach $x=5$ from the right. So we have \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{+}}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n  \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 5}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c82e8ef4-2a15-56e8-b738-07fccda39b3f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c82e8ef4-2a15-56e8-b738-07fccda39b3f" :answer-field/id #uuid "c82e8ef4-2a15-56e8-b738-07fccda39b3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b4617ab1-1384-53f9-b8be-1f00c735f439" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd5573bc-b47f-5f58-a252-b7d45896a9a0" "answer-8728ada0-6c3b-5791-bfb2-4d61763caa83" "answer-5e5604a8-cfd8-5832-a1f4-245805b48104" "answer-8aead3f9-d0d0-5e1d-b8cd-ae8d98f0276f" "answer-b4617ab1-1384-53f9-b8be-1f00c735f439"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd5573bc-b47f-5f58-a252-b7d45896a9a0" :answer/id #uuid "cd5573bc-b47f-5f58-a252-b7d45896a9a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8728ada0-6c3b-5791-bfb2-4d61763caa83" :answer/id #uuid "8728ada0-6c3b-5791-bfb2-4d61763caa83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e5604a8-cfd8-5832-a1f4-245805b48104" :answer/id #uuid "5e5604a8-cfd8-5832-a1f4-245805b48104" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8aead3f9-d0d0-5e1d-b8cd-ae8d98f0276f" :answer/id #uuid "8aead3f9-d0d0-5e1d-b8cd-ae8d98f0276f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4617ab1-1384-53f9-b8be-1f00c735f439" :answer/id #uuid "b4617ab1-1384-53f9-b8be-1f00c735f439" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119871 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a9e5a7d0-a42d-53f5-8ae1-26c9c5fee794" "question-ae5c5c63-a42c-5945-a9b3-a559880f74b2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a9e5a7d0-a42d-53f5-8ae1-26c9c5fee794" :question/id #uuid "a9e5a7d0-a42d-53f5-8ae1-26c9c5fee794" :question/math-academy-id "q-75543" :question/problem "![](images/cc/cc2ea14272a30271bb022e9deb5e8b506ed0c2725d6633e7308b3786cb09d84c.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of $f(x).$ Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "We see from the graph that as $x$ approaches $-1$ from the left, the function $f(x)$ approaches $-\\infty .$ So, the left-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty \\,.\n$$\n\nLikewise, as $x$ approaches $-1$ from the right, the function $f(x)$ again approaches $-\\infty .$ So, the right-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x)=-\\infty \\,.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=-\\infty \\,.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e026018c-c11f-523c-bb59-03bedfd7598b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e026018c-c11f-523c-bb59-03bedfd7598b" :answer-field/id #uuid "e026018c-c11f-523c-bb59-03bedfd7598b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fd423fcc-7cf3-54fa