-b18e-e644408ae0b0" :step/content 17592186284586 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188317 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-25bfd26a-4014-54ec-bb25-41bebf6a0072"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-25bfd26a-4014-54ec-bb25-41bebf6a0072" :question/id #uuid "25bfd26a-4014-54ec-bb25-41bebf6a0072" :question/math-academy-id "q-144847" :question/problem "![](images/86/861e191e0f0b0d993e2d16f29da17ec9e258d657f6bdfc471e5fa9cf21a67b21.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-3,2].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above. Find the maximum value of the function $f(x)$ on the interval $[-3,2]$ given that $f(2)=4.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the maximum value of $f(x)$ on $[-3,2]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval. \n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-3,2),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=-1$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-3,-1,2.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nThe function is made up of $1$ trapezoid and $1$ triangle. Let's add the areas bounded by these shapes to our diagram:\n\n![](images/b7/b7f6e2f43ae474ec3194b2395144e8ea7dc9964da65bd018af08bb24b873bdd4.png)\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =4 \\\\ f(-1) & =f(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{-1}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =f(2)-{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4-5 \\\\  & =-1 \\\\ f(-3) & =f(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{-3}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =f(2)-{\\int }_{-3}^{2}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4-(-1+5) \\\\  & =4-4 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the largest value of $f$ from our candidates. \n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{max}}=max\\{4,-1,0\\}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the maximum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{max}}=4,$ and the value of $x$ that maximizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{max}}=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-920aa12b-f974-5b8f-8512-f6303ba5b5ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-920aa12b-f974-5b8f-8512-f6303ba5b5ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "920aa12b-f974-5b8f-8512-f6303ba5b5ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6ccbd482-6f82-5365-be1b-29c7904b3202" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4dc84bcf-3d54-5493-bbf5-f15198a48f9a" "answer-3cf2092b-4dd8-5577-b36a-cd5c90777daa" "answer-ff533885-694c-5d8f-b455-8987426b0493" "answer-6ccbd482-6f82-5365-be1b-29c7904b3202" "answer-ba49c28a-0d1a-51dd-9f2d-4aaa2b5101b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4dc84bcf-3d54-5493-bbf5-f15198a48f9a" :answer/id #uuid "4dc84bcf-3d54-5493-bbf5-f15198a48f9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cf2092b-4dd8-5577-b36a-cd5c90777daa" :answer/id #uuid "3cf2092b-4dd8-5577-b36a-cd5c90777daa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff533885-694c-5d8f-b455-8987426b0493" :answer/id #uuid "ff533885-694c-5d8f-b455-8987426b0493" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ccbd482-6f82-5365-be1b-29c7904b3202" :answer/id #uuid "6ccbd482-6f82-5365-be1b-29c7904b3202" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba49c28a-0d1a-51dd-9f2d-4aaa2b5101b8" :answer/id #uuid "ba49c28a-0d1a-51dd-9f2d-4aaa2b5101b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188318 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5fcb87aa-38a0-5213-a001-cd7978756f39" "question-df0b416e-f70a-5924-a6c6-f62bc6887f2f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5fcb87aa-38a0-5213-a001-cd7978756f39" :question/id #uuid "5fcb87aa-38a0-5213-a001-cd7978756f39" :question/math-academy-id "q-144875" :question/problem "![](images/cb/cba90791c239c986390a8a7fe1cb3ea0b4abb9cfd86ca13cba9ece6a5b4860b6.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-5,4].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above. Find the minimum value of the function $f(x)$ on the interval $[-5,4]$ given that $f(4)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-5,4]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval. \n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-5,4),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=0.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-5,0,4.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nThe function is made up of $1$ trapezoid and $2$ triangles. Let's add the areas bounded by these shapes to our diagram:\n\n![](images/a8/a8bff8783c0e536cd0e3c475a8fca87a9861a1e1f0ca7f2833ca9c434da2426d.png)\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4) & =1 \\\\ f(0) & =f(4)+{\\int }_{4}^{0}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =f(4)-{\\int }_{0}^{4}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1-(-8) \\\\  & =1+8 \\\\  & =9 \\\\ f(-5) & =f(4)+{\\int }_{4}^{-5}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =f(4)-{\\int }_{-5}^{4}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1-(9+2-8) \\\\  & =1-3 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates. \n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{1,9,-2\\}=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=-2,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=-5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3aff9ed3-8040-515b-8916-8efa69b012c5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3aff9ed3-8040-515b-8916-8efa69b012c5" :answer-field/id #uuid "3aff9ed3-8040-515b-8916-8efa69b012c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-23045462-0c63-5e55-a547-f6d9c1423dc2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-23045462-0c63-5e55-a547-f6d9c1423dc2" "answer-4271de1f-2b94-5b54-9703-cefae48d132f" "answer-6e3a2d1e-d9c5-580c-ac02-4274a8f8aea8" "answer-f3763ea8-131b-51ba-8034-87fce394cdde" "answer-97cf76f8-44e3-5bf4-98db-081710e81c23"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23045462-0c63-5e55-a547-f6d9c1423dc2" :answer/id #uuid "23045462-0c63-5e55-a547-f6d9c1423dc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4271de1f-2b94-5b54-9703-cefae48d132f" :answer/id #uuid "4271de1f-2b94-5b54-9703-cefae48d132f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e3a2d1e-d9c5-580c-ac02-4274a8f8aea8" :answer/id #uuid "6e3a2d1e-d9c5-580c-ac02-4274a8f8aea8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3763ea8-131b-51ba-8034-87fce394cdde" :answer/id #uuid "f3763ea8-131b-51ba-8034-87fce394cdde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97cf76f8-44e3-5bf4-98db-081710e81c23" :answer/id #uuid "97cf76f8-44e3-5bf4-98db-081710e81c23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-df0b416e-f70a-5924-a6c6-f62bc6887f2f" :question/id #uuid "df0b416e-f70a-5924-a6c6-f62bc6887f2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-344165" :question/problem "![](images/73/731237ee8d4ea5fdb53c50971bad11dd9f4317f595ae9af95846b17b6d064fce.png)\n\nThe function $g(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-5,3].$ The graph of ${g}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $g(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the region between the graph and the $x$-axis is $7.$\n\nGiven that $g(3)=4,$ what is the minimum value ${g}_{\\text{min}}$ of $g(x)$ on the interval $[-5,3]?$\n\n${g}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $g(x)$ on $[-5,3]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${g}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-5,3),$ and ${g}^{′}(x)\\ne 0$ inside the interval. Therefore, the candidates are $x=-5,3.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $g$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(3) & =4 \\\\ g(-5) & =g(3)+{\\int }_{3}^{-5}{g}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =g(3)-{\\int }_{-5}^{3}{g}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4-7 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $g$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $g$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{g}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{4,-3\\}=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $g$ is ${g}_{\\text{min}}=-3,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $g(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=-5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9fef5802-c8af-5407-b40d-c7abf62f6135"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9fef5802-c8af-5407-b40d-c7abf62f6135" :answer-field/id #uuid "9fef5802-c8af-5407-b40d-c7abf62f6135" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-964ed659-a234-5d78-b3eb-254df1986447" :answer-field/choices ["answer-964ed659-a234-5d78-b3eb-254df1986447"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-964ed659-a234-5d78-b3eb-254df1986447" :answer/id #uuid "964ed659-a234-5d78-b3eb-254df1986447" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-07f38657-8d82-53c8-a490-bb5a42290b31" :activity/id #uuid "07f38657-8d82-53c8-a490-bb5a42290b31" :activity/title "Further Optimizing Functions Using Graphs of Derivatives" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049623 :activity/course 17592186046673 :activity/steps ["step-0a11be39-e15b-5695-a209-6aa5aa9d56b2" "step-dcee01d3-9728-5373-bd94-47606309bf0a" "step-6c8a0b71-476e-5aff-ab08-21790a69690d"] :activity/first-step "step-0a11be39-e15b-5695-a209-6aa5aa9d56b2" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-0a11be39-e15b-5695-a209-6aa5aa9d56b2" :step/id #uuid "0a11be39-e15b-5695-a209-6aa5aa9d56b2" :step/content "question-25bfd26a-4014-54ec-bb25-41bebf6a0072" :step/next "step-dcee01d3-9728-5373-bd94-47606309bf0a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-dcee01d3-9728-5373-bd94-47606309bf0a" :step/id #uuid "dcee01d3-9728-5373-bd94-47606309bf0a" :step/content "question-5fcb87aa-38a0-5213-a001-cd7978756f39" :step/next "step-6c8a0b71-476e-5aff-ab08-21790a69690d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6c8a0b71-476e-5aff-ab08-21790a69690d" :step/id #uuid "6c8a0b71-476e-5aff-ab08-21790a69690d" :step/content "question-df0b416e-f70a-5924-a6c6-f62bc6887f2f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110734 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0355a074-20a2-5164-b4c8-0cc8e981bffa" "question-14efb3d8-c222-5e12-b8b9-d5a90aefed95"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0355a074-20a2-5164-b4c8-0cc8e981bffa" :question/id #uuid "0355a074-20a2-5164-b4c8-0cc8e981bffa" :question/math-academy-id "q-7234" :question/problem "![](images/2c/2c1790cb306a749737594f994f6893d0146d5f2ed2458dc9e50ff9f4278475d7.png)\n\nThe graph above shows $y=k({3}^{x}).$ What is the value of the constant $k?$" :question/worked-solution "To plot the graph of $y=k({3}^{x})$ we take the graph of $y={3}^{x}$ and stretch it vertically by a scale factor of  $k.$ Under the action of this transformation, the $y$-intercept is mapped from $(0,1)$ to $(0,k)$\n\nComparing the point $(0,1.5)$ on the graph to $(0,k),$ we see that we must have $k=1.5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-19b2167b-179a-512d-a243-20e811f23fa5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-19b2167b-179a-512d-a243-20e811f23fa5" :answer-field/id #uuid "19b2167b-179a-512d-a243-20e811f23fa5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-71905937-3f2a-58cd-8d8a-0bf16a4067cf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3118dc30-430b-5641-935f-ec4dd4e6c1d3" "answer-71905937-3f2a-58cd-8d8a-0bf16a4067cf" "answer-a6023041-ba47-52db-be44-55cee271cb2a" "answer-525e884d-2c1b-5eed-a6de-01b31fd57b53" "answer-ae03e523-d064-5bc8-8d5a-b59524369b9a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3118dc30-430b-5641-935f-ec4dd4e6c1d3" :answer/id #uuid "3118dc30-430b-5641-935f-ec4dd4e6c1d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71905937-3f2a-58cd-8d8a-0bf16a4067cf" :answer/id #uuid "71905937-3f2a-58cd-8d8a-0bf16a4067cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6023041-ba47-52db-be44-55cee271cb2a" :answer/id #uuid "a6023041-ba47-52db-be44-55cee271cb2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-525e884d-2c1b-5eed-a6de-01b31fd57b53" :answer/id #uuid "525e884d-2c1b-5eed-a6de-01b31fd57b53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae03e523-d064-5bc8-8d5a-b59524369b9a" :answer/id #uuid "ae03e523-d064-5bc8-8d5a-b59524369b9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-14efb3d8-c222-5e12-b8b9-d5a90aefed95" :question/id #uuid "14efb3d8-c222-5e12-b8b9-d5a90aefed95" :question/math-academy-id "q-26883" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the graph of $y=6({5}^{x})?$" :question/worked-solution "First we plot the graph of $y={5}^{x}$:\n\n![](images/c0/c0bc33204b0cc8590f93529a76d4dd785fc52317505fcdee4a03022315da5333.png)\n\nThen, we scale this graph vertically by a factor of $6.$ The $y$-intercept becomes $(0,6),$ and the resulting graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/11/11a8b1a124812c91be270a728ce07c3c2a9ea9f5b7bddd351ceb7d7dec7970f7.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-da254e7c-1de1-5549-93d9-35f0de0913ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-da254e7c-1de1-5549-93d9-35f0de0913ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "da254e7c-1de1-5549-93d9-35f0de0913ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-60fabe23-e9a4-511d-a2ac-e20dfc36269c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fe984f0e-babe-53d8-9142-84c87b1f2bf9" "answer-60fabe23-e9a4-511d-a2ac-e20dfc36269c" "answer-920f3fb1-3e7b-5542-a5a0-f6b4897b1c53" "answer-c239bd0b-d1fd-5b79-b1ba-c5658d4f895b" "answer-7b772bde-4db4-5297-93d4-4e70a27f4a4e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe984f0e-babe-53d8-9142-84c87b1f2bf9" :answer/id #uuid "fe984f0e-babe-53d8-9142-84c87b1f2bf9" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/0f/0f667cef87ff35e6012a9b059aec786a7175c49b8e5d5ee473f1648e42638394.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60fabe23-e9a4-511d-a2ac-e20dfc36269c" :answer/id #uuid "60fabe23-e9a4-511d-a2ac-e20dfc36269c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/30/30a6d96c1bf2138e93cb1bdf2b162091c592dcae6aed8ef852e0d5eb382fb699.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-920f3fb1-3e7b-5542-a5a0-f6b4897b1c53" :answer/id #uuid "920f3fb1-3e7b-5542-a5a0-f6b4897b1c53" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/5d/5db9ec3cf9d8597d498b315ba38d28042940d66e08ce677feccfda99464460a9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c239bd0b-d1fd-5b79-b1ba-c5658d4f895b" :answer/id #uuid "c239bd0b-d1fd-5b79-b1ba-c5658d4f895b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/7f/7f3210b5790d2a553bf0