pe/math :answer/value "x<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f09c79c9-533f-56c9-9850-3e6d0f52fcf8" :answer/id #uuid "f09c79c9-533f-56c9-9850-3e6d0f52fcf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-019635f7-41ec-5c33-956d-3525d5f504ee" :answer/id #uuid "019635f7-41ec-5c33-956d-3525d5f504ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da0adfae-34a6-5d88-a719-1f51cf3b61e3" :answer/id #uuid "da0adfae-34a6-5d88-a719-1f51cf3b61e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-d5568308-bda7-5799-8026-2f5cbd870b6e" :activity/id #uuid "d5568308-bda7-5799-8026-2f5cbd870b6e" :activity/title "Graphing Exponential Growth Functions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048789 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-50ca0270-94b5-532f-bb51-0054a50b67eb" "step-e4f415bb-254a-5692-963e-82a207e52a4a" "step-52733f46-8218-5aeb-b8b9-bbaf5b7ced19"] :activity/first-step "step-50ca0270-94b5-532f-bb51-0054a50b67eb" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-50ca0270-94b5-532f-bb51-0054a50b67eb" :step/id #uuid "50ca0270-94b5-532f-bb51-0054a50b67eb" :step/content "question-0355a074-20a2-5164-b4c8-0cc8e981bffa" :step/next "step-e4f415bb-254a-5692-963e-82a207e52a4a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e4f415bb-254a-5692-963e-82a207e52a4a" :step/id #uuid "e4f415bb-254a-5692-963e-82a207e52a4a" :step/content "question-14efb3d8-c222-5e12-b8b9-d5a90aefed95" :step/next "step-52733f46-8218-5aeb-b8b9-bbaf5b7ced19" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-52733f46-8218-5aeb-b8b9-bbaf5b7ced19" :step/id #uuid "52733f46-8218-5aeb-b8b9-bbaf5b7ced19" :step/content "question-7782f625-0fd2-5a62-8065-db81e75a2462" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162155 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d05ba4df-d0b9-5ab9-9679-a4617e87b3ef" "question-3efec416-c341-5cd9-8d7e-9c91c7f8fc1f" "question-5ad1bec0-7cb2-5524-90ce-c8dd7afd9873" "question-e322b76b-ff51-56ef-b559-1a8882734867"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d05ba4df-d0b9-5ab9-9679-a4617e87b3ef" :question/id #uuid "d05ba4df-d0b9-5ab9-9679-a4617e87b3ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-163603" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.75$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $P(X=0,Y=2)=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=2)$\n\nII. $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent" :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=0,Y=2)=f(0,2)=0.15.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=2)={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2)=0.6\\cdot 0.25=0.15.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Checking all other possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,4) & =0.45=0.6\\cdot 0.75={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(4) & ✓ \\\\ f(1,2) & =0.1=0.4\\cdot 0.25={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓ \\\\ f(1,4) & =0.3=0.4\\cdot 0.75={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(4) & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ must be independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-52c90bc9-5310-58df-8a7a-9bd5771aabfb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-52c90bc9-5310-58df-8a7a-9bd5771aabfb" :answer-field/id #uuid "52c90bc9-5310-58df-8a7a-9bd5771aabfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0445cf07-339e-533c-8d42-e149c6fc2cbe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-621af6a9-adbe-50db-806c-fe5e8f2b32bb" "answer-0bc56465-1d50-5315-918d-4e291db03326" "answer-0445cf07-339e-533c-8d42-e149c6fc2cbe" "answer-55420914-c12f-5597-a7c1-3b23dc38ce54" "answer-68910a4f-8fa8-58d5-afc0-03e3a87b1e22"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-621af6a9-adbe-50db-806c-fe5e8f2b32bb" :answer/id #uuid "621af6a9-adbe-50db-806c-fe5e8f2b32bb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bc56465-1d50-5315-918d-4e291db03326" :answer/id #uuid "0bc56465-1d50-5315-918d-4e291db03326" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0445cf07-339e-533c-8d42-e149c6fc2cbe" :answer/id #uuid "0445cf07-339e-533c-8d42-e149c6fc2cbe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55420914-c12f-5597-a7c1-3b23dc38ce54" :answer/id #uuid "55420914-c12f-5597-a7c1-3b23dc38ce54" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68910a4f-8fa8-58d5-afc0-03e3a87b1e22" :answer/id #uuid "68910a4f-8fa8-58d5-afc0-03e3a87b1e22" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3efec416-c341-5cd9-8d7e-9c91c7f8fc1f" :question/id #uuid "3efec416-c341-5cd9-8d7e-9c91c7f8fc1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-162826" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.38$ | $0.32$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.02$ | $0.28$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $P(X=0,Y=1)=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=1)$\n\nII. $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent" :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=0,Y=1)=f(0,1)=0.32.$ However, \n\n$$\nP(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=1)={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1)=0.7\\cdot 0.6=0.42.\\,\\times\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nP(X=0,Y=1)\\ne P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=1),\n$$\n\nand $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cbd75960-a5dc-507f-9c7b-443c5b7e70cb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cbd75960-a5dc-507f-9c7b-443c5b7e70cb" :answer-field/id #uuid "cbd75960-a5dc-507f-9c7b-443c5b7e70cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0b9d0c57-960a-50ad-8fa7-9d10ca6901e1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2ccbb2ec-9296-5be5-baf9-880ebc4a387f" "answer-c92f5681-4932-52f0-ad86-222d7ef82f18" "answer-84d27243-3576-50aa-aba0-4aa1d2550b22" "answer-a73d0423-625d-5c20-8c7f-7d3f2dd4cd92" "answer-0b9d0c57-960a-50ad-8fa7-9d10ca6901e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ccbb2ec-9296-5be5-baf9-880ebc4a387f" :answer/id #uuid "2ccbb2ec-9296-5be5-baf9-880ebc4a387f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c92f5681-4932-52f0-ad86-222d7ef82f18" :answer/id #uuid "c92f5681-4932-52f0-a