nter\">$0.4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $P(X=0,Y=1)=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=1)$\n\nII. $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent" :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=0,Y=1)=f(0,1)=0.3.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=1)={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1)=0.6\\cdot 0.5=0.3.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Checking some possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,2) & =0.15\\ne 0.6\\cdot 0.3={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c6c7aa94-526c-5068-b2c9-6d8c4ba852ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c6c7aa94-526c-5068-b2c9-6d8c4ba852ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6c7aa94-526c-5068-b2c9-6d8c4ba852ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-025fce0b-097b-5731-a74e-5ae7056d6398" :answer-field/choices ["answer-437956a9-2047-5bcd-80f5-8a0239806bdd" "answer-32991881-c8fb-5dc7-bdb3-41ca8ebbdef3" "answer-025fce0b-097b-5731-a74e-5ae7056d6398" "answer-c5470c69-c4ff-596e-ab51-bfd9340f48f3" "answer-01e932aa-df02-5ddf-9c65-deb82d4c7df1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-437956a9-2047-5bcd-80f5-8a0239806bdd" :answer/id #uuid "437956a9-2047-5bcd-80f5-8a0239806bdd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32991881-c8fb-5dc7-bdb3-41ca8ebbdef3" :answer/id #uuid "32991881-c8fb-5dc7-bdb3-41ca8ebbdef3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-025fce0b-097b-5731-a74e-5ae7056d6398" :answer/id #uuid "025fce0b-097b-5731-a74e-5ae7056d6398" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5470c69-c4ff-596e-ab51-bfd9340f48f3" :answer/id #uuid "c5470c69-c4ff-596e-ab51-bfd9340f48f3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01e932aa-df02-5ddf-9c65-deb82d4c7df1" :answer/id #uuid "01e932aa-df02-5ddf-9c65-deb82d4c7df1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162388 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5dd8077d-1403-5bd2-b29d-34936c801dde" "question-86447238-489f-5596-b009-12655e2594dd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5dd8077d-1403-5bd2-b29d-34936c801dde" :question/id #uuid "5dd8077d-1403-5bd2-b29d-34936c801dde" :question/math-academy-id "q-143329" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.11$ | $0.44$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.09$ | $0.36$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $P(X=0,Y=1)=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=1)$\n\nII. $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent" :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.11$ | $0.44$ | $0.55$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.09$ | $0.36$ | $0.45$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.2$ | $0.8$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=0,Y=1)=f(0,1)=0.11.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=1)={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1)=0.55\\cdot 0.2=0.11.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Checking all other possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,2) & =0.44=0.55\\cdot 0.8={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓ \\\\ f(1,1) & =0.09=0.45\\cdot 0.2={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓ \\\\ f(1,2) & =0.36=0.45\\cdot 0.8={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ must be independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f0c463fc-1015-5085-92f8-1bd4d3071032"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f0c463fc-1015-5085-92f8-1bd4d3071032" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0c463fc-1015-5085-92f8-1bd4d3071032" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-65a140a9-45f0-5e30-b05a-59065a2072cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4af19015-99ba-5b62-a940-6de9e9bbcfba" "answer-0ea91f7c-b404-57ce-b26b-09691c505bf7" "answer-6600c5ed-cae9-564e-9fb1-8fa6c43b7f48" "answer-65a140a9-45f0-5e30-b05a-59065a2072cb" "answer-5b7d5284-3afb-5213-bddf-0f8f5b688a59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4af19015-99ba-5b62-a940-6de9e9bbcfba" :answer/id #uuid "4af19015-99ba-5b62-a940-6de9e9bbcfba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ea91f7c-b404-57ce-b26b-09691c505bf7" :answer/id #uuid "0ea91f7c-b404-57ce-b26b-09691c505bf7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6600c5ed-cae9-564e-9fb1-8fa6c43b7f48" :answer/id #uuid "6600c5ed-cae9-564e-9fb1-8fa6c43b7f48" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65a140a9-45f0-5e30-b05a-59065a2072cb" :answer/id #uuid "65a140a9-45f0-5e30-b05a-59065a2072cb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b7d5284-3afb-5213-bddf-0f8f5b688a59" :answer/id #uuid "5b7d5284-3afb-5213-bddf-0f8f5b688a59" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-86447238-489f-5596-b009-12655e2594dd" :question/id #uuid "86447238-489f-5596-b009-12655e2594dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-143436" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.7$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $P(X=3,Y=2)=P(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)$\n\nII. $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent" :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.7$ | $0.1$ | $0.8$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.8$ | $0.2$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=3,Y=2)=f(3,2)=0.1.$ However, \n\n$$\nP(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2)=0.2\\cdot 0.8=0.16.\\,\\times\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nP(X=3,Y=2)\\ne P(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2),\n$$\n\nand $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c9a7c0fb-9ef9-5eb1-9b4f-38bbe8edbdcb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c9a7c0fb-9ef9-5eb1-9b4f-38bbe8edbdcb" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9a7c0fb-9ef9-5eb1-9b4f-38bbe8edbdcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b09ee838-ec83-5170-b0f1-28570d5a0b7e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-15cf2687-956c-5a04-a0e5-2aa85321d477" "answer-5796432d-3e16-5dac-aa46-18f20d2fd823" "answer-dcbe36f5-f029-58af-b6c8-d0c6956746a7" "answer-2092959b-1b46-5391-a673-2f6b71e1a7f1" "answer-b09ee838-ec83-5170-b0f1-28570d5a0b7e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15cf2687-956c-5a04-a0e5-2aa85321d477" :answer/id #uuid "15cf2687-956c-5a04-a0e5-2aa85321d477" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5796432d-3e16-5dac-aa46-18f20d2fd823" :answer/id #uuid "5796432d-3e16-5dac-aa46-18f20d2fd823" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcbe36f5-f029-58af-b6c8-d0c6956746a7" :answer/id #uuid "dcbe36f5-f029-58af-b6c8-d0c6956746a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2092959b-1b46-5391-a673-2f6b71e1a7f1" :answer/id #uuid "2092959b-1b46-5391-a673-2f6b71e1a7f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b09ee838-ec83-5170-b0f1-28570d5a0b7e" :answer/id #uuid "b09ee838-ec83-5170-b0f1-28570d5a0b7e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162154 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-38788558-45ed-5ac8-b24c-5c511e7f90ed" "question-1200d290-e6bf-5cb3-acb4-bada082b8f96" "question-1222ccd8-a96c-520b-9c55-3b7bc8a21989"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-38788558-45ed-5ac8-b24c-5c511e7f90ed" :question/id #uuid "38788558-45ed-5ac8-b24c-5c511e7f90ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-162902" :question/problem "The partially complete joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the independent discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=5$ | $Y=7$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.09$ | $0.36$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=4$ | $∗$ | $∗$ | $0.55$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $?$ | $∗$ | $1$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $P(Y=5)?$" :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, since our random variables are independent, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,5) & ={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(5) \\\\ P(X=2,Y=5) & =P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=5) \\\\ 0.09 & =0.45\\cdot P(Y=5) \\\\ P(Y=5) & =\\frac{0.09}{0.45} \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cbc1988e-2e0c-53fc-9f2e-80ceecb51b3d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cbc1988e-2e0c-53fc-9f2e-80ceecb51b3d" :answer-field/id #uuid "cbc1988e-2e0c-53fc-9f2e-80ceecb51b3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a099181c-9c17-5544-8a65-42b3b9368d19" :answer-field/choices ["answer-19aa25ad-336b-5766-a733-09397663c89a" "answer-2545460e-d87d-59a9-896f-f4804c477441" "answer-a099181c-9c17-5544-8a65-42b3b9368d19" "answer-7f50fbea-844a-5239-b2f9-f71e2cc1ef2c" "answer-efebf525-cba0-577d-92c8-aacdbfe1f3b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19aa25ad-336b-5766-a733-09397663c89a" :answer/id #uuid "19aa25ad-336b-5766-a733-09397663c89a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2545460e-d87d-59a9-896f-f4804c477441" :answer/id #uuid "2545460e-d87d-59a9-896f-f4804c477441" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a099181c-9c17-5544-8a65-42b3b9368d19" :answer/id #uuid "a099181c-9c17-5544-8a65-42b3b9368d19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f50fbea-844a-5239-b2f9-f71e2cc1ef2c" :answer/id #uuid "7f50fbea-844a-5239-b2f9-f71e2cc1ef2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efebf525-cba0-577d-92c8-aacdbfe1f3b3" :answer/id #uuid "efebf525-cba0-577d-92c8-aacdbfe1f3b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1200d290-e6bf-5cb3-acb4-bada082b8f96" :question/id #uuid "1200d290-e6bf-5cb3-acb4-bada082b8f96" :question/math-academy-id "q-149649" :question/problem "The marginal mass functions of the independent discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are shown below. Given that the corresponding joint probability mass function is $f(x,y),$ find $f(2,5).$\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th></tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, since our discrete random variables are independent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,5) & ={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(5) \\\\  & =0.2\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5c35ad51-9dbb-5b36-83e3-01a4846b5800"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5c35ad51-9dbb-5b36-83e3-01a4846b5800" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c35ad51-9dbb-5b36-83e3-01a4846b5800" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5392d1d8-0ead-5406-b4da-fc7f65455500" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9009a014-79e2-5f7f-b4a9-236a79c15e16" "answer-5392d1d8-0ead-5406-b4da-fc7f65455500" "answer-71fff1b0-8e0b-5d4f-b9b9-0f9b67b6b928" "answer-3228beb4-ad50-531c-b488-d73c9985ee19" "answer-a7b587ec-54f7-53f1-bb48-172fcb853d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9009a014-79e2-5f7f-b4a9-236a79c15e16" :answer/id #uuid "9009a014-79e2-5f7f-b4a9-236a79c15e16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.08" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5392d1d8-0ead-5406-b4da-fc7f65455500" :answer/id #uuid "5392d1d8-0ead-5406-b4da-fc7f65455500" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71fff1b0-8e0b-5d4f-b9b9-0f9b67b6b928" :answer/id #uuid "71fff1b0-8e0b-5d4f-b9b9-0f9b67b6b928" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3228beb4-ad50-531c-b488-d73c9985ee19" :answer/id #uuid "3228beb4-ad50-531c-b488-d73c9985ee19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7b587ec-54f7-53f1-bb48-172fcb853d10" :answer/id #uuid "a7b587ec-54f7-53f1-bb48-172fcb853d10" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Impossible to determine using the given information." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1222ccd8-a96c-520b-9c55-3b7bc8a21989" :question/id #uuid "1222ccd8-a96c-520b-9c55-3b7bc8a21989" :question/math-academy-id "q-149655" :question/problem "The marginal mass functions of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are shown below. Given that the corresponding joint probability mass function is $f(x,y),$ find $f(6,4).$\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.65$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Since we don't know whether $X$ and $Y$ are independent, it is impossible to determine the joint distribution of $X$ and $Y$ using only the given information." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-47dc876f-fe20-575f-9f83-7dfac231f314"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-47dc876f-fe20-575f-9f83-7dfac231f314" :answer-field/id #uuid "47dc876f-fe20-575f-9f83-7dfac231f314" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0fbc3c76-06e3-5bcf-a5f8-8ef75b6a0b52" :answer-field/choices ["answer-693f3501-9ea8-52a8-b120-f969af9507c2" "answer-84cfd073-9456-54ff-bfb1-9ff4d427e723" "answer-2137f84b-7e04-5e1f-b4e8-004de4b809f5" "answer-00e0926c-dc16-5c6f-aef8-a5999f210009" "answer-0fbc3c76-06e3-5bcf-a5f8-8ef75b6a0b52"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-693f3501-9ea8-52a8-b120-f969af9507c2" :answer/id #uuid "693f3501-9ea8-52a8-b120-f969af9507c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.105" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-