b/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ae574887-66dc-55be-86f5-550b61aba1dd" :step/id #uuid "ae574887-66dc-55be-86f5-550b61aba1dd" :step/content 17592186504625 :step/next "step-0bda8fd9-13f2-5c84-b50a-70fa5ee8f0e8" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0bda8fd9-13f2-5c84-b50a-70fa5ee8f0e8" :step/id #uuid "0bda8fd9-13f2-5c84-b50a-70fa5ee8f0e8" :step/content 17592186243968 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124659 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e645c316-71e4-58c2-8dda-54dfd003d3ee"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e645c316-71e4-58c2-8dda-54dfd003d3ee" :question/id #uuid "e645c316-71e4-58c2-8dda-54dfd003d3ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-90968" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+6x-8?$" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny=a{x}^{2}+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=-1<0,$ $b=6,$ and $c=-8.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the parabola opens downward. Consequently, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}=-\\frac{6}{2\\cdot (-1)}=3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=3$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-{x}^{2}+6x-8 \\\\  & =-(3)^{2}+6(3)-8 \\\\  & =-9+18-8 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(3,1),$ and the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,1].$\n\n![](images/36/362626b55b357f91efb0fc89a51361bd8a9be368a6645becd3db07580accaaff.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4e87ba1c-6874-5d0a-996a-3c1acc628a9e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4e87ba1c-6874-5d0a-996a-3c1acc628a9e" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e87ba1c-6874-5d0a-996a-3c1acc628a9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-403b07c6-f056-5c1e-9ced-36e0c1b0f3fd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6c2b3537-03e7-553c-8206-65bd50cf13a8" "answer-403b07c6-f056-5c1e-9ced-36e0c1b0f3fd" "answer-60cc0af6-8ea4-53b5-b553-6a9490590d4c" "answer-fc5e05d0-d612-5386-a5a0-a3bf0dde0b77" "answer-cf772beb-dd46-5ca1-b434-51819c40e211"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c2b3537-03e7-553c-8206-65bd50cf13a8" :answer/id #uuid "6c2b3537-03e7-553c-8206-65bd50cf13a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-403b07c6-f056-5c1e-9ced-36e0c1b0f3fd" :answer/id #uuid "403b07c6-f056-5c1e-9ced-36e0c1b0f3fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60cc0af6-8ea4-53b5-b553-6a9490590d4c" :answer/id #uuid "60cc0af6-8ea4-53b5-b553-6a9490590d4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,3]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc5e05d0-d612-5386-a5a0-a3bf0dde0b77" :answer/id #uuid "fc5e05d0-d612-5386-a5a0-a3bf0dde0b77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-3,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf772beb-dd46-5ca1-b434-51819c40e211" :answer/id #uuid "cf772beb-dd46-5ca1-b434-51819c40e211" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124584 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8a71e9cb-8bb6-5c17-8cab-a2b0b8515a29" "question-87522f6e-547f-5501-803f-38e69a4ab8bc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8a71e9cb-8bb6-5c17-8cab-a2b0b8515a29" :question/id #uuid "8a71e9cb-8bb6-5c17-8cab-a2b0b8515a29" :question/math-academy-id "q-90979" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)=-3(x+1)^{2}-7?$" :question/worked-solution "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=-1$ and $k=-7,$ the vertex is $(-1,-7).$\n\n- Since $a=-3<0,$ the parabola opens downwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens downwards, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output. \n\nTherefore, the range is $(-\\infty ,-7].$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/21/21049fc3aa8d6e2b64c4fd5db723c00e5878473ad8b96f25271c46edc48ed3ea.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e59cc3b3-2d1b-5a47-a0da-cf1c94d9ece9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e59cc3b3-2d1b-5a47-a0da-cf1c94d9ece9" :answer-field/id #uuid "e59cc3b3-2d1b-5a47-a0da-cf1c94d9ece9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dcf18488-82e6-55f7-bc88-70816d80833f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-892d7645-442d-5314-b45a-7ea9f816363b" "answer-97d84504-9c16-5ada-9158-d437803d7880" "answer-dcf18488-82e6-55f7-bc88-70816d80833f" "answer-6f449186-68af-505d-8ba1-e89490d3588a" "answer-812ca881-ad52-5c82-8b1a-ad9ec2c3192f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-892d7645-442d-5314-b45a-7ea9f816363b" :answer/id #uuid "892d7645-442d-5314-b45a-7ea9f816363b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97d84504-9c16-5ada-9158-d437803d7880" :answer/id #uuid "97d84504-9c16-5ada-9158-d437803d7880" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcf18488-82e6-55f7-bc88-70816d80833f" :answer/id #uuid "dcf18488-82e6-55f7-bc88-70816d80833f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-7]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f449186-68af-505d-8ba1-e89490d3588a" :answer/id #uuid "6f449186-68af-505d-8ba1-e89490d3588a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-812ca881-ad52-5c82-8b1a-ad9ec2c3192f" :answer/id #uuid "812ca881-ad52-5c82-8b1a-ad9ec2c3192f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[-7,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-87522f6e-547f-5501-803f-38e69a4ab8bc" :question/id #uuid "87522f6e-547f-5501-803f-38e69a4ab8bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-106283" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)=-2(x+13)^{2}+14?$" :question/worked-solution "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=-13$ and $k=14,$ the vertex is $(-13,14).$\n\n- Since $a=-2<0,$ the parabola opens downwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens downwards, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output. \n\nTherefore, the range is $(-\\infty ,14].$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/08/08b2ebf2fb3ecb8e02eed81d47e349dad22bde0d97e8920fabc75a8e2301da2b.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-27b48aea-ee27-5772-a6cc-4c2cfba244bb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-27b48aea-ee27-5772-a6cc-4c2cfba244bb" :answer-field/id #uuid "27b48aea-ee27-5772-a6cc-4c2cfba244bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9b259075-8cb8-5df3-945a-7a9c6ac033fd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4b63033a-24e2-5903-b295-91cc93bb9990" "answer-9b259075-8cb8-5df3-945a-7a9c6ac033fd" "answer-f1daca14-4c4e-530e-9222-4e3f4ba8d119" "answer-dc78e2b3-11f1-573d-b784-24f309474acc" "answer-eaf2fb45-750e-5cdd-afa7-44f40ee5659d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b63033a-24e2-5903-b295-91cc93bb9990" :answer/id #uuid "4b63033a-24e2-5903-b295-91cc93bb9990" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,13]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b259075-8cb8-5df3-945a-7a9c6ac033fd" :answer/id #uuid "9b259075-8cb8-5df3-945a-7a9c6ac033fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,14]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1daca14-4c4e-530e-9222-4e3f4ba8d119" :answer/id #uuid "f1daca14-4c4e-530e-9222-4e3f4ba8d119" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[13,14]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc78e2b3-11f1-573d-b784-24f309474acc" :answer/id #uuid "dc78e2b3-11f1-573d-b784-24f309474acc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[13,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eaf2fb45-750e-5cdd-afa7-44f40ee5659d" :answer/id #uuid "eaf2fb45-750e-5cdd-afa7-44f40ee5659d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[14,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124660 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fb786a48-6efc-557e-bdac-ba3e5bfceb11"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-fb786a48-6efc-557e-bdac-ba3e5bfceb11" :question/id #uuid "fb786a48-6efc-557e-bdac-ba3e5bfceb11" :question/math-academy-id "q-250655" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $f(x)=-(x+7)(x+9).$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$<f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny=a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}),\n$$\n\nwith $a=-1<0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the parabola opens downward. Consequently, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-9$ and ${x}_{2}=-7,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{-9-7}{2}=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=-8$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-(x+7)(x+9) \\\\  & =-(-8+7)(-8+9) \\\\  & =-(-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-8,1),$ and the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,1],$ i.e. $-\\infty <f(x)\\le 1.$\n\n![](images/0c/0cb245de80be7125a1e8874781ed21fc2845f25f7ee8e1e43356819f87fe1b6c.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-53804295-71ff-5921-a1f0-85877fe7f459" "answer-field-24a33357-db32-588d-8f62-a8e54ad0fed1" "answer-field-16033fcf-6425-52d7-842c-b314f27cbd64"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-53804295-71ff-5921-a1f0-85877fe7f459" :answer-field/id #uuid "53804295-71ff-5921-a1f0-85877fe7f459" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-66d81624-7ec5-5cda-a1be-d41d2b795a4a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-66d81624-7ec5-5cda-a1be-d41d2b795a4a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66d81624-7ec5-5cda-a1be-d41d2b795a4a" :answer/id #uuid "66d81624-7ec5-5cda-a1be-d41d2b795a4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-24a33357-db32-588d-8f62-a8e54ad0fed1" :answer-field/id #uuid "24a33357-db32-588d-8f62-a8e54ad0fed1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-991ba2b0-831a-53eb-b183-63a7aa87cc69" :answer-field/choices ["answer-991ba2b0-831a-53eb-b183-63a7aa87cc69"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-991ba2b0-831a-53eb-b183-63a7aa87cc69" :answer/id #uuid "991ba2b0-831a-53eb-b183-63a7aa87cc69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-16033fcf-6425-52d7-842c-b314f27cbd64" :answer-field/id #uuid "16033fcf-6425-52d7-842c-b314f27cbd64" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3eeca0e1-b6de-52ef-a755-30e10b649fb4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3eeca0e1-b6de-52ef-a755-30e10b649fb4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3eeca0e1-b6de-52ef-a755-30e10b649fb4" :answer/id #uuid "3eeca0e1-b6de-52ef-a755-30e10b649fb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-5985754e-714a-5c2c-b300-e0ee4263e5d0" :activity/id #uuid "5985754e-714a-5c2c-b300-e0ee4263e5d0" :activity/title "Domain and Range of Quadratic Functions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049828 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-7095dfca-d543-5340-966b-1a6ee03b8d50" "step-b221606f-e40b-54aa-b16e-e307f3403f69" "step-665ef093-e5bb-5ba9-9e9a-d396adc7f6c4" "step-a0240a55-8160-5d0a-b1e1-609611199c9d" "step-30cad7c6-2bfe-57a8-8544-4f6a46441b2e"] :activity/first-step "step-7095dfca-d543-5340-966b-1a6ee03b8d50" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-7095dfca-d543-5340-966b-1a6ee03b8d50" :step/id #uuid "7095dfca-d543-5340-966b-1a6ee03b8d50" :step/content 17592186124875 :step/next "step-b221606f-e40b-54aa-b16e-e307f3403f69" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b221606f-e40b-54aa-b16e-e307f3403f69" :step/id #uuid "b221606f-e40b-54aa-b16e-e307f3403f69" :step/content "question-e645c316-71e4-58c2-8dda-54dfd003d3ee" :step/next "step-665ef093-e5bb-5ba9-9e9a-d396adc7f6c4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-665ef093-e5bb-5ba9-9e9a-d396adc7f6c4" :step/id #uuid "665ef093-e5bb-5ba9-9e9a-d396adc7f6c4" :step/content "question-8a71e9cb-8bb6-5c17-8cab-a2b0b8515a29" :step/next "step-a0240a55-8160-5d0a-b1e1-609611199c9d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a0240a55-8160-5d0a-b1e1-609611199c9d" :step/id #uuid "a0240a55-8160-5d0a-b1e1-609611199c9d" :step/content "question-87522f6e-547f-5501-803f-38e69a4ab8bc" :step/next "step-30cad7c6-2bfe-57a8-8544-4f6a46441b2e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-30cad7c6-2bfe-57a8-8544-4f6a46441b2e" :step/id #uuid "30cad7c6-2bfe-57a8-8544-4f6a46441b2e" :step/content "question-fb786a48-6efc-557e-bdac-ba3e5bfceb11" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059678 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f67b31bd-a1c3-55b5-a439-944a03b0aa36"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f67b31bd-a1c3-55b5-a439-944a03b0aa36" :question/id #uuid "f67b31bd-a1c3-55b5-a439-944a03b0aa36" :question/math-academy-id "q-105266" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ for $y=7x-4{x}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7x-4{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =7-2\\cdot 4x \\\\  & =7-8x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7-8x) \\\\  & =0-8 \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9a4cd441-2d73-575a-8e4f-cf616f00a6cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9a4cd441-2d73-575a-8e4f-cf616f00a6cf" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a4cd441-2d73-575a-8e4f-cf616f00a6cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-73cccaa9-1469-5106-8f3a-4e7dc596b43b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-feb0e40d-3168-5f79-9621-a08d68c75d15" "answer-73cccaa9-1469-5106-8f3a-4e7dc596b43b" "answer-43acf527-aa43-56a4-a96a-58ef4e28a8e9" "answer-584a6d9d-1fb0-5bdb-b29c-e22ab95fc9c9" "answer-56a0a88f-a8ae-5f65-9f3a-27a2c63d48a5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-feb0e40d-3168-5f79-9621-a08d68c75d15" :answer/id #uuid "feb0e40d-3168-5f79-9621-a08d68c75d15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73cccaa9-1469-5106-8f3a-4e7dc596b43b" :answer/id #uuid "73cccaa9-1469-5106-8f3a-4e7dc596b43b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43acf527-aa43-56a4-a96a-58ef4e28a8e9" :answer/id #uuid "43acf527-aa43-56a4-a96a-58ef4e28a8e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-584a6d9d-1fb0-5bdb-b29c-e22ab95fc9c9" :answer/id #uuid "584a6d9d-1fb0-5bdb-b29c-e22ab95fc9c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-8x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56a0a88f-a8ae-5f65-9f3a-27a2c63d48a5" :answer/id #uuid "56a0a88f-a8ae-5f65-9f3a-27a2c63d48a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7-8x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059679 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-224e49e4-5633-5d71-8ad0-69cc905bfd6e" "question-30675b2a-1249-5c56-916f-1fdddcd8a518"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-224e49e4-5633-5d71-8ad0-69cc905bfd6e" :question/id #uuid "224e49e4-5633-5d71-8ad0-69cc905bfd6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-104295" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=\\frac{5-{x}^{4}}{6{x}^{2}},$ find ${f}^{‴}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can rewrite the function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{5-{x}^{4}}{6{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6{x}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5}{6{x}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5}{6}{x}^{-2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{-3}-\\frac{x}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{-3}-\\frac{x}{3}) \\\\  & =5{x}^{-4}-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{-4}-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =-20{x}^{-5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{20}{{x}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e6989b96-6453-5959-889b-dc271201d958"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e6989b96-6453-5959-889b-dc271201d958" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6989b96-6453-5959-889b-dc271201d958" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-647a3429-1e9b-544a-b9d3-11c5d9d3589c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-74dab907-e9f0-5710-95ca-4bdd3d7d778f" "answer-647a3429-1e9b-544a-b9d3-11c5d9d3589c" "answer-3378bb16-2914-549c-88df-2501f5000303" "answer-2b069f17-e412-5356-a860-81ca222aa729" "answer-1612e9ba-4706-5213-9e4d-cb6b22726949"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74dab907-e9f0-5710-95ca-4bdd3d7d778f" :answer/id #uuid "74dab907-e9f0-5710-95ca-4bdd3d7d778f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{x}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-647a3429-1e9b-544a-b9d3-11c5d9d3589c" :answer/id #uuid "647a3429-1e9b-544a-b9d3-11c5d9d3589c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{20}{{x}^{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3378bb16-2914-549c-88df-2501f5000303" :answer/id #uuid "3378bb16-2914-549c-88df-2501f5000303" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3{x}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b069f17-e412-5356-a860-81ca222aa729" :answer/id #uuid "2b069f17-e412-5356-a860-81ca222aa729" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{20}{3{x}^{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1612e9ba-4706-5213-9e4d-cb6b22726949" :answer/id #uuid "1612e9ba-4706-5213-9e4d-cb6b22726949" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-30675b2a-1249-5c56-916f-1fdddcd8a518" :question/id #uuid "30675b2a-1249-5c56-916f-1fdddcd8a518" :question/math-academy-id "q-343087" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3x,$ we have\n\n${f}^{‴}(x)=$ \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3x) \\\\  & =x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3) \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fae03ebe-384c-56a0-b28b-7e7a4779e500"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fae03ebe-384c-56a0-b28b-7e7a4779e500" :answer-field/id #uuid "fae03ebe-384c-56a0-b28b-7e7a4779e500" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d8882614-1542-5cb1-8585-441d502aa822" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d8882614-1542-5cb1-8585-441d502aa822"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8882614-1542-5cb1-8585-441d502aa822" :answer/id #uuid "d8882614-1542-5cb1-8585-441d502aa822" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\cos x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060897 :tutorial/content "The **second derivative**  is the derivative of a function's first derivative. It is written as $f''(x).$\n\nTo calculate the second derivative of a function $f(x)$, we first need to calculate the first derivative $f'(x).$ After that, we calculate the derivative of $f'(x).$ So using prime $\\left('\\right)$ notation, we can define the second derivative of a function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf''(x) = (f'(x))'.\n$$\n\nLet's try it out with the function $f(x) = 4x^2 + 3x.$ The first derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(4{x}^{2}+3x)^{′} \\\\  & =4(2)x+3 \\\\  & =8x+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now calculate the derivative of $f'(x)$ to give us $f''(x).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =({f}^{′}(x))^{′} \\\\  & =(8x+3)^{′} \\\\  & =8+0 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the second derivative of $f(x)$ is $8.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060899 :tutorial/content "To calculate the third derivative of the function $f(x)=2x^4+3x,$ we need to differentiate it three times.\n\nComputing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{4}+3x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4{x}^{4-1}+1\\cdot 3{x}^{1-1} \\\\ \\text{ } & =8{x}^{3}+3{x}^{0} \\\\  & =8{x}^{3}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{x}^{3}+3) \\\\  & =8\\cdot 3{x}^{3-1}+0 \\\\ \\text{ } & =24{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(24{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =24\\cdot 2{x}^{2-1} \\\\ \\text{ } & =48x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the third derivative of $f(x)$ is $f'''(x)=48x.$ \n\nUsing Leibniz notation, the third derivative of a function $f(x)$ can also be written as\n\n$$\nf'''(x)=\\dfrac {\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}\\left(\\dfrac {\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}\\left(\\dfrac {\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(f(x))\\right)\\right)=\\dfrac {\\textrm d^3}{\\textrm d x^3}f(x).\n$$\n\nIn general, if we want to calculate the $n$-th order derivative of a function, we need to differentiate it $n$ times:\n\n$$\nf^{(n)}(x)=\\dfrac {\\textrm d^n}{\\textrm d x^n}f(x).\n$$\n\n**Note**: The parenthesis in the superscript of $f^{(n)}(x)$ means that it is the the $n$-th derivative of $f(x).$ This is to distinguish it from $f^n(x)$ with no parenthesis, which indicates the $n$-th power of $f(x).$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059952 :activity/expected-seconds 780.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129242 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-822263d6-7f5d-5a37-a89e-f93c0b6eb7bf" "question-eab5bcd3-8a73-5188-a5f4-a81be3ecb0f7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-822263d6-7f5d-5a37-a89e-f93c0b6eb7bf" :question/id #uuid "822263d6-7f5d-5a37-a89e-f93c0b6eb7bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-39499" :question/problem "![](images/ad/ad5f193a1ff21e03659789473a6e4918b6dd7ba25cd9db4e6fc0f729d0481391.png)\n\nWhat are the equations of the horizontal asymptotes of $y=f(x)$ whose graph is shown above?" :question/worked-solution "- On the right of the graph, we see that as $x$ gets larger and larger, the function $f(x)$ levels off to the value of $-3.$ We can express this as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)\\to -3\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\infty\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has a horizontal asymptote at $y=-3.$\n\n- On the left of the graph, we see that as $x$ gets more and more negative, the function $f(x)$ levels off to the value of $2.$ We can express this as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)\\to 2\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to -\\infty\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ also has a horizontal asymptote at $y=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b11bf33c-db38-51a0-bd44-1b88637ccbd5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b11bf33c-db38-51a0-bd44-1b88637ccbd5" :answer-field/id #uuid "b11bf33c-db38-51a0-bd44-1b88637ccbd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-91cba4ea-e346-546d-ace3-bcbdd6893c8b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-88d595c6-1012-5a5a-9e6f-6b68cfbbc410" "answer-41b6ea5c-ab1b-5a16-9523-3c6e933226f6" "answer-76e8c735-8556-5d88-ae45-fc7b24307d2a" "answer-91cba4ea-e346-546d-ace3-bcbdd6893c8b" "answer-6376518c-7e22-57ce-b405-b13cfe25c801"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88d595c6-1012-5a5a-9e6f-6b68cfbbc410" :answer/id #uuid "88d595c6-1012-5a5a-9e6f-6b68cfbbc410" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-3$ and $x=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41b6ea5c-ab1b-5a16-9523-3c6e933226f6" :answer/id #uuid "41b6ea5c-ab1b-5a16-9523-3c6e933226f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-3$ and $x=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76e8c735-8556-5d88-ae45-fc7b24307d2a" :answer/id #uuid "76e8c735-8556-5d88-ae45-fc7b24307d2a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$y=-3$ and $y=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91cba4ea-e346-546d-ace3-bcbdd6893c8b" :answer/id #uuid "91cba4ea-e346-546d-ace3-bcbdd6893c8b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$y=-3$ and $y=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6376518c-7e22-57ce-b405-b13cfe25c801" :answer/id #uuid "6376518c-7e22-57ce-b405-b13cfe25c801" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The function has no horizontal asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129243 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ba3e1985-7070-5883-9f3a-6c38d6b3795b" "question-994cad67-228c-54a3-8cec-2145c453420a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ba3e1985-7070-5883-9f3a-6c38d6b3795b" :question/id #uuid "ba3e1985-7070-5883-9f3a-6c38d6b3795b" :question/math-academy-id "q-39517" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8f7dead46db0b268a9474ad842d8d6077cc84971895e005a3686ab5b18131b6c.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is given above. Find $a$ such that $f(x)\\to a$ as $x\\to \\infty .$" :question/worked-solution "On the right of the graph, we see that as $x$ gets larger and larger, the function $f(x)$ levels off to the value of $1.$ We can express this as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)\\to 1\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\infty\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0d9a3e9d-c479-5cb4-a591-1e8fc50740e2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0d9a3e9d-c479-5cb4-a591-1e8fc50740e2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d9a3e9d-c479-5cb4-a591-1e8fc50740e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2935108b-6e9f-5435-b8b4-fb38e0a0a09a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d74dd0a-fdd6-5862-8570-0a7f632a6b12" "answer-081f5a61-028e-52f7-9bb4-cddbe719e3c3" "answer-8a557587-3fb3-5568-a8f7-10cd9e5ed062" "answer-2935108b-6e9f-5435-b8b4-fb38e0a0a09a" "answer-20cc55df-bf81-5643-9e10-2dfd34c40f4e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d74dd0a-fdd6-5862-8570-0a7f632a6b12" :answer/id #uuid "4d74dd0a-fdd6-5862-8570-0a7f632a6b12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-081f5a61-028e-52f7-9bb4-cddbe719e3c3" :answer/id #uuid "081f5a61-028e-52f7-9bb4-cddbe719e3c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a557587-3fb3-5568-a8f7-10cd9e5ed062" :answer/id #uuid "8a557587-3fb3-5568-a8f7-10cd9e5ed062" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2935108b-6e9f-5435-b8b4-fb38e0a0a09a" :answer/id #uuid "2935108b-6e9f-5435-b8b4-fb38e0a0a09a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20cc55df-bf81-5643-9e10-2dfd34c40f4e" :answer/id #uuid "20cc55df-bf81-5643-9e10-2dfd34c40f4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-994cad67-228c-54a3-8cec-2145c453420a" :question/id #uuid "994cad67-228c-54a3-8cec-2145c453420a" :question/math-academy-id "q-47463" :question/problem "![](images/74/7471044234ec20534f33abb45d26db3c0a2876bed0fcc73844d1867b354491c0.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true for the graph shown above?\n\nI. $f(x)\\to 2$ as $x\\to -\\infty$\n\nII. $f(x)\\to 1$ as $x\\to \\infty$\n\nIII. $f(x)\\to 0$ as $x\\to -\\infty$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement one-by-one.\n\n- On the left of the graph, we see that as $x$ gets more and more negative, the function $f(x)$ levels off to the value of $2.$ We can express this as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)\\to 2\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to -\\infty\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true while statement III is false.\n\n- On the right of the graph, we see that as $x$ gets larger and larger, the function $f(x)$ levels off to the value of $1.$ We can express this as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)\\to 1\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\infty\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement II is true.\n\nAs a result, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a3cb9a42-0764-519a-825c-1ba27120adab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a3cb9a42-0764-519a-825c-1ba27120adab" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3cb9a42-0764-519a-825c-1ba27120adab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5fe23007-a46a-5c1e-a688-b89de9dd4d36" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5fe23007-a46a-5c1e-a688-b89de9dd4d36" "answer-7a1b6905-3792-5373-bed5-087a9a37fe83" "answer-73f835ab-97b9-5393-9c3f-ad23fb2c1220" "answer-32f92ea6-8864-5f96-80c4-672e19e420e9" "answer-168eec9d-d998-5fcf-a223-3b5d62da107e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fe23007-a46a-5c1e-a688-b89de9dd4d36" :answer/id #uuid "5fe23007-a46a-5c1e-a688-b89de9dd4d36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a1b6905-3792-5373-bed5-087a9a37fe83" :answer/id #uuid "7a1b6905-3792-5373-bed5-087a9a37fe83" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73f835ab-97b9-5393-9c3f-ad23fb2c1220" :answer/id #uuid "73f835ab-97b9-5393-9c3f-ad23fb2c1220" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32f92ea6-8864-5f96-80c4-672e19e420e9" :answer/id #uuid "32f92ea6-8864-5f96-80c4-672e19e420e9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-168eec9d-d998-5fcf-a223-3b5d62da107e" :answer/id #uuid "168eec9d-d998-5fcf-a223-3b5d62da107e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-eab5bcd3-8a73-5188-a5f4-a81be3ecb0f7" :question/id #uuid "eab5bcd3-8a73-5188-a5f4-a81be3ecb0f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-75999" :question/problem "![](images/c1/c12deadd41a9c2853d0d2d50ba5c19ac6ca13012d7672941c92fa5e6cc5df642.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true for the graph shown above?\n\nI. $y=-1$ is a horizontal asymptote of $f(x)$\n\nII. $y=1$ is a horizontal asymptote of $f(x)$\n\nIII. $y=2$ is a horizontal asymptote of $f(x)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement one-by-one.\n\n- On the right of the graph, we see that as $x$ gets larger and larger, the function $f(x)$ levels off to the value of $1.$ We can express this as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)\\to 1\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\infty\n$$\n\nThis means that $y=1$ is a horizontal asymptote of $f(x).$ Therefore, statement II is true.\n\n- On the left of the graph, we see that as $x$ gets more and more negative, the function $f(x)$ levels off to the value of $2.$ We can express this as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)\\to 2\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to -\\infty .\n$$\n\nThis means that $y=2$ is a horizontal asymptote of $f(x).$ Therefore, III is also true.\n\n- The horizontal asymptotes of $f(x)$ are $y=1$ and $y=2.$ The line $y=-1$ is not a horizontal asymptote of $f(x)$ because the function does not level off to $-1$ on the right nor on the left. Therefore, I is false.\n\nAs a result, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a23871ce-bc15-5531-bf06-ef1d19b4fac1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a23871ce-bc15-5531-bf06-ef1d19b4fac1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a23871ce-bc15-5531-bf06-ef1d19b4fac1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0aa107fd-e1ce-52f6-894f-3a9f5aabc4f6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f4659fb3-0e2d-5310-bd05-4a261c0df905" "answer-cf780927-5af4-57b4-8b56-612429cbc9b4" "answer-fb1290f7-00c0-5b91-ab44-213a5c8aa6b7" "answer-0aa107fd-e1ce-52f6-894f-3a9f5aabc4f6" "answer-3242475e-44a7-57f1-a086-a119e64b8342"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4659fb3-0e2d-5310-bd05-4a261c0df905" :answer/id #uuid "f4659fb3-0e2d-5310-bd05-4a261c0df905" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf780927-5af4-57b4-8b56-612429cbc9b4" :answer/id #uuid "cf780927-5af4-57b4-8b56-612429cbc9b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb1290f7-00c0-5b91-ab44-213a5c8aa6b7" :answer/id #uuid "fb1290f7-00c0-5b91-ab44-213a5c8aa6b7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0aa107fd-e1ce-52f6-894f-3a9f5aabc4f6" :answer/id #uuid "0aa107fd-e1ce-52f6-894f-3a9f5aabc4f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3242475e-44a7-57f1-a086-a119e64b8342" :answer/id #uuid "3242475e-44a7-57f1-a086-a119e64b8342" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-e13664e1-acc2-5e26-9aa9-cb80edddc807" :activity/id #uuid "e13664e1-acc2-5e26-9aa9-cb80edddc807" :activity/title "End Behavior of Functions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050255 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-05d1b5f7-911e-5855-8309-87882fbd1201" "step-4227861c-86ff-5688-a73a-852c46fa515d" "step-c15f7f38-970a-5da3-816b-d00e38b1d089" "step-1af9142f-e256-5a70-bedb-9d90883fc27a"] :activity/first-step "step-05d1b5f7-911e-5855-8309-87882fbd1201" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-05d1b5f7-911e-5855-8309-87882fbd1201" :step/id #uuid "05d1b5f7-911e-5855-8309-87882fbd1201" :step/content "question-822263d6-7f5d-5a37-a89e-f93c0b6eb7bf" :step/next "step-4227861c-86ff-5688-a73a-852c46fa515d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4227861c-86ff-5688-a73a-852c46fa515d" :step/id #uuid "4227861c-86ff-5688-a73a-852c46fa515d" :step/content "question-ba3e1985-7070-5883-9f3a-6c38d6b3795b" :step/next "step-c15f7f38-970a-5da3-816b-d00e38b1d089" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c15f7f38-970a-5da3-816b-d00e38b1d089" :step/id #uuid "c15f7f38-970a-5da3-816b-d00e38b1d089" :step/content "question-994cad67-228c-54a3-8cec-2145c453420a" :step/next "step-1af9142f-e256-5a70-bedb-9d90883fc27a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1af9142f-e256-5a70-bedb-9d90883fc27a" :step/id #uuid "1af9142f-e256-5a70-bedb-9d90883fc27a" :step/content "question-eab5bcd3-8a73-5188-a5f4-a81be3ecb0f7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115289 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1d85a230-c47c-5ffa-b563-dedfdd86c871"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1d85a230-c47c-5ffa-b563-dedfdd86c871" :question/id #uuid "1d85a230-c47c-5ffa-b563-dedfdd86c871" :question/math-academy-id "q-28074" :question/problem "Which of the following curves is generated by $y=-3(x+2)(x+1)(x-1)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the function is a product of $3$ linear binomials, so this function is a cubic function. Moreover, it is a negative cubic because if we were to expand the parentheses, the coefficient of the ${x}^{3}$ term would be negative:\n\n$$\n-3(x+2)(x+1)(x-1)=-3x\\cdot x\\cdot x+⋯=-3{x}^{3}+⋯\n$$\n\nThe equation is given in the factored form. So by the zero-product rule, we deduce that the roots are  $x=-2,$ $x=-1,$ and $x=1.$ \n\nWe now find the $y$-intercept of the curve by plugging the value $x=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3(0+2)(0+1)(0-1) \\\\  & =-3(2)(1)(-1) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we draw an $\\text{S}$-shaped graph that passes through the three roots $x=-2,-1,1$ and has the $y$-intercept $y=6,$ as follows:\n\n![](images/47/472cf0dd7807c15e8e8334a163d1cfbfbbdcd974534e99b94222929048e72b31.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c9f032b0-b93a-57ee-ab00-0ed6113f8ef6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c9f032b0-b93a-57ee-ab00-0ed6113f8ef6" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9f032b0-b93a-57ee-ab00-0ed6113f8ef6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d124ec48-3b27-5a60-951a-d15de5d7a40d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ad8813ef-4396-5a21-9fdd-ad55cb9aa352" "answer-d0a6cbb4-361d-51df-86ce-cc6151d8155e" "answer-d124ec48-3b27-5a60-951a-d15de5d7a40d" "answer-84d8beff-2479-5088-bdac-e141e015a59c" "answer-a68e71cf-7bb8-52ab-aecd-7b06a8b6b148"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad8813ef-4396-5a21-9fdd-ad55cb9aa352" :answer/id #uuid "ad8813ef-4396-5a21-9fdd-ad55cb9aa352" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/13/13c3fb2aadb027fe3397b237e8c8027e1fcc7418106cc488e51f81062fa75e2e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0a6cbb4-361d-51df-86ce-cc6151d8155e" :answer/id #uuid "d0a6cbb4-361d-51df-86ce-cc6151d8155e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/18/18a34470ca210b12544b90b520dfc4d2ed443231f55a2443ffbbdf31e72d61c1.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d124ec48-3b27-5a60-951a-d15de5d7a40d" :answer/id #uuid "d124ec48-3b27-5a60-951a-d15de5d7a40d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/47/472cf0dd7807c15e8e8334a163d1cfbfbbdcd974534e99b94222929048e72b31.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84d8beff-2479-5088-bdac-e141e015a59c" :answer/id #uuid "84d8beff-2479-5088-bdac-e141e015a59c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/56/56f52c1e31d4e6224a222bdc57ee726848672332b7e1e6bed0c7d51db09a4f60.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a68e71cf-7bb8-52ab-aecd-7b06a8b6b148" :answer/id #uuid "a68e71cf-7bb8-52ab-aecd-7b06a8b6b148" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/7b/7b5f467f84f0c7d8b3c1dce432ae0c4db8117cde6730611ac4e48881a0bb4b69.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115291 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2c01baff-ab5f-57ff-be23-ce994353bbde"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2c01baff-ab5f-57ff-be23-ce994353bbde" :question/id #uuid "2c01baff-ab5f-57ff-be23-ce994353bbde" :question/math-academy-id "q-28365" :question/problem "Given that $x=2$ is a root of $f(x)=-{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-14x+8,$ which of the following curves is generated by $y=f(x)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that the function is a negative cubic curve because the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is negative.\n\nWe are told that $x=2$ is a root of $f(x),$ which means that $(x-2)$ is a factor of $f(x).$ So, to find the other roots of $f(x)$ we use synthetic division to divide $f(x)$ by $(x-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 2 & -1 & 7 & -14 & 8 \\\\  &  & -2 & 10 & -8 \\\\  & -1 & 5 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(x-2)(-{x}^{2}+5x-4) \\\\  & =-(x-2)({x}^{2}-5x+4) \\\\  & =-(x-2)(x-1)(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the factors equal to zero, we find that the other roots of $f(x)$ are $x=1$ and $x=4.$ \n\nNow, let's find the $y$-intercept. To do that, we substitute $x=0,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-(0-2)(0-1)(0-4) \\\\  & =-(-2)(-1)(-4) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we draw an $S$-shaped graph that passes through the three roots $x=1,2,4$ and has the $y$-intercept $y=8,$ as follows:\n\n![](images/21/21dec37151f40778b8f094d3ae68cd8716c993535e53496cf7f148817c72e345.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4d149e3a-5f29-5983-a00c-27e7be6451ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4d149e3a-5f29-5983-a00c-27e7be6451ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d149e3a-5f29-5983-a00c-27e7be6451ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-376e8047-36e1-5ce3-92f5-7608828fe9a4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0ecb6cc8-9b1a-53ec-8594-8c498c333227" "answer-f972b644-cb9f-5d42-8c7d-406b85ac2b37" "answer-376e8047-36e1-5ce3-92f5-7608828fe9a4" "answer-d264c026-fbc5-505c-b381-13549290748d" "answer-01480b4d-e433-5319-b7dd-b2b93fad7110"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ecb6cc8-9b1a-53ec-8594-8c498c333227" :answer/id #uuid "0ecb6cc8-9b1a-53ec-8594-8c498c333227" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/12/1222fb6503f602a7da1b84d73fa8ced3474ae7f65b695d9e71fba267712278b4.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f972b644-cb9f-5d42-8c7d-406b85ac2b37" :answer/id #uuid "f972b644-cb9f-5d42-8c7d-406b85ac2b37" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/19/19a0cce27a712f55a6430100fe29d4ea1a323709f1a398fc2ce48c1b4fe3206b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-376e8047-36e1-5ce3-92f5-7608828fe9a4" :answer/id #uuid "376e8047-36e1-5ce3-92f5-7608828fe9a4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/21/21dec37151f40778b8f094d3ae68cd8716c993535e53496cf7f148817c72e345.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d264c026-fbc5-505c-b381-13549290748d" :answer/id #uuid "d264c026-fbc5-505c-b381-13549290748d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/84/8468568ef0a3848797191a51080e0a904f9a739f659286358341bb218012fb43.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01480b4d-e433-5319-b7dd-b2b93fad7110" :answer/id #uuid "01480b4d-e433-5319-b7dd-b2b93fad7110" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/e3/e38995dc7545fe0b32a7214438397304b0fc2a3dd3b589f387ad7230b7740ee9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115288 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1fbfa8ab-6879-57fc-b2d0-196f095281bf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1fbfa8ab-6879-57fc-b2d0-196f095281bf" :question/id #uuid "1fbfa8ab-6879-57fc-b2d0-196f095281bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-112004" :question/problem "Given that $(x+3)$ is a factor of $f(x)={x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-9x-18,$ which of the following curves is generated by $y=f(x)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the function is a positive cubic curve because the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is positive.\n\nWe are told that $(x+3)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ so to find the other roots of $f(x)$ we use synthetic division to divide $f(x)$ by  $(x+3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2 & -9 & -18 \\\\  &  & -3 & 3 & 18 \\\\  & 1 & -1 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(x+3)({x}^{2}-x-6) \\\\  & =(x+3)(x+2)(x-3),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the roots of $f(x)$ are $x=-3,$ $x=-2,$ and $x=3.$ \n\nNow, let's find the $y$-intercept. To do that, we substitute $x=0,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(0+3)(0+2)(0-3) \\\\  & =(3)(2)(-3) \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we draw an inverted $\\text{S}$-shaped graph that passes through the three roots $x=-3,-2,3$ and has the $y$-intercept $y=-18,$ as follows:\n\n![](images/c3/c3d41c300747f4f0f18607351f2f03241c9a789ed70fe72e05c5a385b708c4c8.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b18f2373-d103-568e-a398-52c15fa56a75"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b18f2373-d103-568e-a398-52c15fa56a75" :answer-field/id #uuid "b18f2373-d103-568e-a398-52c15fa56a75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-acc28117-8c7e-5014-8d43-cf71987edfa5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ceaf2707-9a91-54ce-8aa8-a46bf55db815" "answer-10c54f81-76b6-583f-90ea-fedd6ed4be72" "answer-acc28117-8c7e-5014-8d43-cf71987edfa5" "answer-17b7e3ec-839e-5536-aba8-7da932732eea" "answer-a21448ea-448b-5f5d-8fa7-410e5c305b6b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ceaf2707-9a91-54ce-8aa8-a46bf55db815" :answer/id #uuid "ceaf2707-9a91-54ce-8aa8-a46bf55db815" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/01/016b5bc1171471bb3ce678031ce7cac74187cc06333bd4646ba09b9be054c4e5.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10c54f81-76b6-583f-90ea-fedd6ed4be72" :answer/id #uuid "10c54f81-76b6-583f-90ea-fedd6ed4be72" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/06/066d0669762137e2e014c2b76c941bdf7812c2d537ae1c03e0ae89a1d7107dc3.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-acc28117-8c7e-5014-8d43-cf71987edfa5" :answer/id #uuid "acc28117-8c7e-5014-8d43-cf71987edfa5" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/5c/5cd54c55d39003033450f9cbf0ba1fbcfc6608fd18a50b97b8a23880e2bf25d2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17b7e3ec-839e-5536-aba8-7da932732eea" :answer/id #uuid "17b7e3ec-839e-5536-aba8-7da932732eea" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/aa/aadabdf5e3da853c5d80a902717c0e4e7b7628f63ec45690acb35c9ea1471026.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a21448ea-448b-5f5d-8fa7-410e5c305b6b" :answer/id #uuid "a21448ea-448b-5f5d-8fa7-410e5c305b6b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/dc/dc808580cd0a7dfee4d03a2357d278076650da7acdbe0b963c944ec1338ca66c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-8e96de79-87d9-54d2-95f8-f4785b140574" :activity/id #uuid "8e96de79-87d9-54d2-95f8-f4785b140574" :activity/title "Graphing Cubic Curves Containing Three Distinct Real Roots" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048691 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-95c410e0-d5ac-51fe-bc83-3557448ebd94" "step-2446ca1c-5282-5cff-a939-7255d0f9c35b" "step-cfcb7580-8426-5081-ac0a-40fc40360751"] :activity/first-step "step-95c410e0-d5ac-51fe-bc83-3557448ebd94" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-95c410e0-d5ac-51fe-bc83-3557448ebd94" :step/id #uuid "95c410e0-d5ac-51fe-bc83-3557448ebd94" :step/content "question-1d85a230-c47c-5ffa-b563-dedfdd86c871" :step/next "step-2446ca1c-5282-5cff-a939-7255d0f9c35b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2446ca1c-5282-5cff-a939-7255d0f9c35b" :step/id #uuid "2446ca1c-5282-5cff-a939-7255d0f9c35b" :step/content "question-2c01baff-ab5f-57ff-be23-ce994353bbde" :step/next "step-cfcb7580-8426-5081-ac0a-40fc40360751" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-cfcb7580-8426-5081-ac0a-40fc40360751" :step/id #uuid "cfcb7580-8426-5081-ac0a-40fc40360751" :step/content "question-1fbfa8ab-6879-57fc-b2d0-196f095281bf" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083191 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6dff94b8-5d8c-56b5-9363-d9107e29b4d1" "question-17bccb94-8027-5ec1-b42e-ebe5775a61ec" "question-2b65f25b-10a0-5e3f-8752-11a285fdf596"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6dff94b8-5d8c-56b5-9363-d9107e29b4d1" :question/id #uuid "6dff94b8-5d8c-56b5-9363-d9107e29b4d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-15811" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $y$ on the graph $y=|x+4|-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that $y=|x-h|+k$ is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $h$ units right and $k$ units up.\n\nThe function $y=|x+4|-1$ has $h=-4$ and $k=-1.$ Therefore, it is a translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $4$ units *left* and $1$ unit *down*.\n\n![](images/45/45411bac1f347093b8b9931e1f8f8bee4f1eb411b6256a4c56d0ba33cffe603e.png)\n\nLooking at the graph, we can see that the minimum value of $y$ is $-1.$ This occurs at the point $(-4,-1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3f1dab20-875a-5ecd-83ee-e9779ffd70fb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3f1dab20-875a-5ecd-83ee-e9779ffd70fb" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f1dab20-875a-5ecd-83ee-e9779ffd70fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-091b549b-9482-5c9d-99a3-414abc46226c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-091b549b-9482-5c9d-99a3-414abc46226c" "answer-e8201c4f-d73c-5a75-aee0-069d79e730fa" "answer-96ce8727-2f4f-5e50-b3b2-f6937e57145d" "answer-04656707-2a2c-5ffa-bbcb-9540a7b1d0c7" "answer-9cff91ed-11f3-5a4c-b5a3-c02c22d2774b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-091b549b-9482-5c9d-99a3-414abc46226c" :answer/id #uuid "091b549b-9482-5c9d-99a3-414abc46226c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8201c4f-d73c-5a75-aee0-069d79e730fa" :answer/id #uuid "e8201c4f-d73c-5a75-aee